ª|+<‡˘@Ω°ëxºÆ“ó<"‰Q<Z«=<#¢º)≈WºcIΩF%ºË-º€>⁄<KóÂªô/Üº19m=∂F-ºís√º»/4º¢mëº≥√àª°⁄Ω¨‚ΩÎoéºªì«<BΩ~—ç<7ô<È…<ÖÑªã$Ò∫¨–ﬂº°»^<Ùº<˛~4ªK©Ωr#˛<∞¯∂<Ä'º∞/ù<hâIº^¸<~øÍªsë 9˜‘=/J4Ω€>⁄ªó†;‚1<(¯<’'J∫ıwèºI¡<ı@©∂r5°<—6Y<C#–<së <ÿ)Ç;Ã •ªQâ≤</ÅΩıeÏº∞¡Pªë;ó†ºMº"@˚:iSø<‚1<SØ—º∂ÿ‡∫å…£ºgˆ9<jØh;ı@©º¡Öîº€u@<iºñ-Œ<{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS GASTROC\u00d3LICAS:Gastrocolic fistulas are abnormal connections that can develop between the stomach and colon, often as a complication of gastrostomy."}{"title": "DESCOLOCACI\u00d3N INADVERTIDA DE LA SONDA:Inadvertent dislocation of the tube can lead to obstruction of the gastric outlet tract or displacement into the gastrocutaneous fistula tract."}{"title": "NEDC TRANSPIL\u00d3RICA:NEDC transpiloric refers to a method of nutrient delivery that may require the use of infusion pumps in specific patient populations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS DE 1-6 A\u00d1OS:Children aged 1-6 years have specific dietary requirements, including a daily intake of 1100 ml of nutrition."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS DE 6-7 A 10 A\u00d1OS:Children aged 6-10 years have specific dietary requirements, including a daily intake of 1300 ml of nutrition."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS MAYORES DE 10 A\u00d1OS:Children over 10 years have specific dietary requirements, including a daily intake of 1500 to 2000 ml of nutrition."}{"title": "SEGHNP:SEGHNP, the Spanish Society of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition, is an organization dedicated to advancing pediatric nutrition standards. It collaborates with SENPE to develop and enhance guidelines related to pediatric nutrition, ensuring that best practices are established and followed in the field. Through its efforts, SEGHNP plays a crucial role in shaping the nutritional care and guidelines for children."}{"title": "ANECIPN:ANECIPN is the National Association of Pediatric Nutrition Specialists in Spain, dedicated to the field of pediatric enteral nutrition. The organization collaborates with SENPE and SEGHNP to establish and promote standards for enteral nutrition, ensuring that best practices are followed in the care of pediatric patients."}{"title": "SECP:The SECP, or Spanish Society of Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, is an organization that plays a significant role in the consensus on pediatric enteral nutrition, collaborating closely with SENPE. It is dedicated to establishing and promoting standards for pediatric nutrition, ensuring that best practices are followed in clinical settings."}{"title": "PEDR\u00d3N GINER C:Pedr\u00f3n Giner C is a prominent figure in the field of pediatric nutrition, recognized for his significant contributions to both enteral and parenteral nutrition literature. He is a co-author of a consensus document on pediatric parenteral nutrition published in the journal Nutr Hosp. Additionally, he has played a vital role in developing guidelines and literature related to pediatric enteral nutrition, demonstrating his expertise and commitment to improving nutritional practices for children. His extensive writing on these topics underscores his influence and dedication to advancing knowledge in pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "MORO VILLARES JM:Moreno Villares JM is a co-author engaged in pediatric nutrition research and standardization. In addition to this role, he also addresses the ethical aspects of nutrition and hydration in children, contributing to a comprehensive understanding of these critical issues in pediatric care."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO EN GASTROENTEROLOG\u00cdA, HEPATOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N PEDI\u00c1TRICA:A comprehensive treatment guide that includes enteral nutrition as a key component for managing pediatric gastroenterological and nutritional issues."}{"title": "TABLAS:The entity \"TABLAS\" refers to tables included in a document that serve multiple purposes related to nutrition. These tables provide diagnostic parameters for assessing the severity of malnutrition, offering essential criteria for evaluation. Additionally, they outline the main indications for enteral nutrition in pediatrics, detailing various medical conditions and their corresponding nutritional requirements. Together, these tables serve as a comprehensive resource for understanding and addressing nutritional needs in both malnutrition assessment and enteral nutrition guidance for pediatric patients."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES PARA LA INGESTI\u00d3N:A category of conditions that impede the ability to ingest food, necessitating enteral nutrition in pediatric patients."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES PARA LA DIGESTI\u00d3N Y ABSORCI\u00d3N:A category of conditions that affect digestion and nutrient absorption, often requiring enteral nutrition interventions in pediatric care."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES EXTRADIGESTIVAS:A category of diseases outside the digestive system that can increase nutritional requirements, often necessitating enteral nutrition in pediatric patients."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD ONCOL\u00d3GICA:The entity \"ENFERMEDAD ONCOL\u00d3GICA\" refers to a type of cancer that can significantly impact the nutritional status of patients, particularly pediatric patients undergoing treatment. This condition may necessitate specialized nutritional support, including enteral nutrition, to address the nutritional needs of these young patients. Additionally, \"ENFERMEDAD ONCOL\u00d3GICA\" is associated with an increased prevalence of malnutrition, especially in advanced stages of the disease. This highlights the critical importance of nutritional management in the care of individuals affected by cancer."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL PREOPERATORIA:Preoperative enteral nutrition aimed at improving the nutritional status of pediatric patients before surgery.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ COSTA C:Mart\u00ednez Costa C is a notable figure in the field of pediatric nutrition, recognized for their contributions to various aspects of this specialty. They are a co-author of a consensus document on pediatric parenteral nutrition, which was published in the journal Nutr Hosp. Additionally, Mart\u00ednez Costa C has collaborated on research concerning enteral nutrition in pediatrics, further demonstrating their expertise in this area. Their work also encompasses a range of topics related to nutritional assessment and pediatric nutrition, highlighting their commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in the field."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL PEDI\u00c1TRICA:NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL PEDI\u00c1TRICA is a chapter discussing pediatric parenteral nutrition, its administration, and guidelines."}{"title": "NE CONTINUA:NE continua refers to the continuous enteral nutrition administration method discussed in the document, outlining its initiation and progression based on age groups."}{"title": "VITORIA:Vitoria is one of the authors contributing to the chapter on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "L\u00d3PEZ-BRIZ:L\u00f3pez-Briz is one of the authors contributing to the chapter on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "RIBES SI\u00d3N:Ribes Si\u00f3n is one of the authors contributing to the chapter on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CAROLINA FUENTES SI\u00d3N:Carolina Fuentes Si\u00f3n is one of the authors contributing to the chapter on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "R. SANCH\u00cdS:R. Sanch\u00eds is one of the authors contributing to the chapter on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "C. GUTI\u00c9RREZ:C. Guti\u00e9rrez is one of the authors contributing to the chapter on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "J. DALMAU:J. Dalmau is one of the authors contributing to the chapter on pediatric parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL CENTRAL:Nutritional therapy that accesses circulation through a large-caliber vein using a central venous catheter"}{"title": "CVC:CVC, or Central Venous Catheter, is a medical device designed for various clinical applications, primarily for administering medication, fluids, and parenteral nutrition. It is particularly utilized in acute situations and critical care settings, allowing for long-term intravenous access to the vascular system. CVCs are essential for delivering treatments and drawing blood samples, making them a vital tool in patient management.\n\nHowever, the use of CVCs is not without risks. They can experience thrombotic obstructions and are associated with potential infections, which are significant concerns in their application. Overall, CVCs play a crucial role in modern medical practice, especially for patients requiring sustained intravenous therapy."}{"title": "BROVIAC:Another type of tunneled catheter used for long-term venous access"}{"title": "GROSHONG:GROSHONG refers to a type of central venous catheter specifically designed for long-term venous access. This catheter is engineered to minimize the risk of infection and thrombosis, making it a preferred choice for patients requiring extended intravenous therapy."}{"title": "PICC:PICC, or Peripherally Inserted Central Catheter, is a specialized type of central venous catheter designed for insertion into a peripheral vein. It is primarily utilized for longer-term parenteral nutrition, allowing for effective access to the venous system. The PICC provides a reliable means of accessing veins for various medical treatments, making it an essential tool in patient care."}{"title": "ANESTESIA Y REANIMACI\u00d3N:Department responsible for ensuring the placement and management of catheters"}{"title": "RADIOLOG\u00cdA PEDI\u00c1TRICA INTERVENCIONISTA:Interventional pediatric radiology department involved in catheter placement"}{"title": "EDAD:EDAD, which stands for \"Elderly Demographic Age Data,\" plays a crucial role in understanding age-related health considerations. It provides recommendations for catheter sizes and fluid intake tailored to the needs of older patients. Furthermore, EDAD is identified as a significant predictor of the necessity for enteral nutrition, especially in individuals aged 80 years and older. This highlights the importance of age in influencing surgical outcomes and underscores the need for age-specific medical strategies."}{"title": "CLORHEXIDINA:Chlorhexidine is a versatile antiseptic widely utilized for various disinfection purposes. It is employed for skin disinfection prior to surgical procedures and for sterilizing surgical instruments, ensuring a sterile environment in medical settings. Additionally, chlorhexidine is used for disinfection before venipuncture, making it essential in clinical practices. Furthermore, it serves an important role in oral hygiene, particularly for patients in critical care settings, helping to maintain oral health and prevent infections. Overall, chlorhexidine is a crucial antiseptic in both surgical and healthcare environments."}{"title": "INFLAMACI\u00d3N:Inflammation is a physiological response that serves as a common complication associated with venous access. It can significantly impact the nutritional status of patients, particularly those with chronic kidney disease. This response plays a crucial role in the body's healing processes but can also lead to adverse effects in certain medical conditions."}{"title": "FLEBITIS:Phlebitis is a common complication associated with venous access"}{"title": "AP\u00d3SITO EST\u00c9RIL TRANSPARENTE:Sterile transparent dressings are used to protect catheters from infections and injuries"}{"title": "TAMA\u00d1O DEL CAT\u00c9TER:Recommendations for catheter size based on patient age"}{"title": "SOLUCIONES CON L\u00cdPIDOS:Lipid solutions used to decrease the osmolarity of parenteral nutrition"}{"title": "PROTOCOL DE MANEJO DEL CAT\u00c9TER:Protocol for catheter management and treatment of complications)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "FIEBRE:FIEBRE, or fever, is a clinical condition characterized by an increase in body temperature. This condition can lead to heightened energy expenditure, particularly in pediatric patients, which may subsequently elevate their nutritional requirements. Fever often accompanies acute diarrhea and serves as an important indicator for conducting stool cultures in specific situations. In hospitalized children, fever can significantly impact their nutritional treatment by increasing both energy and fluid needs."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA:Insuficiencia cardiaca is a medical condition characterized by the heart's inability to pump blood sufficiently to meet the body's needs. This condition often leads to fluid retention and various complications. It is commonly associated with heart disease and may necessitate adjustments in fluid and nutrient administration, particularly in the context of parenteral nutrition for children."}{"title": "EDMAS:EDMAS refers to the presence of edema, a condition that can complicate the assessment of nutritional status in patients. Edema can influence the fluid and electrolyte needs in children, thereby affecting their nutritional treatment. It is also a clinical manifestation of congestive heart failure, which is associated with sodium and water retention. Additionally, edema can be a sign of malnutrition, particularly in patients with celiac disease if not properly managed."}{"title": "AMINOSTERIL-N HEPA:A specialized amino acid solution used for patients with liver failure."}{"title": "NEPHROTECT:A specialized amino acid solution used for patients with renal failure in anuria."}{"title": "CLORO:CLORO, also known as chloride, is a vital mineral and electrolyte that plays a crucial role in maintaining the body's electrolyte balance and fluid regulation. It is typically found in the body at levels ranging from 98 to 106 mEq/l. The recommended daily intake of chloride varies by age, with specific dietary reference intake levels outlined in health guidelines for different age groups, including pediatric patients.\n\nChloride is particularly important in the care of neonates, where it is managed alongside sodium and potassium levels. It is an essential component of parenteral nutrition solutions, which are critical for maintaining acid-base balance and fluid balance in patients who cannot receive nutrition through traditional means. In pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition, chloride is required in specific amounts to support their growth and development.\n\nAdditionally, CLORO is utilized in medical treatments, especially in cases of metabolic alkalosis, highlighting its significance in various therapeutic contexts. Overall, chloride is an indispensable electrolyte necessary for numerous bodily functions, including the maintenance of acid-base balance and fluid homeostasis."}{"title": "LIPOFUNDINA:LIPOFUNDINA is a brand of lipid emulsion specifically designed for use in parenteral nutrition. It is a 20% fat emulsion that combines soybean oil and medium-chain triglycerides, which enhances tolerance, particularly in newborns. This mixed lipid preparation, introduced in the late 1980s, consists of a balanced formulation of 50% medium-chain triglycerides and 50% long-chain triglycerides derived from soybean oil. LIPOFUNDINA serves to meet the lipid requirements in pediatric nutrition, making it a vital component in intravenous nutrition therapies."}{"title": "SMOFLIPID:SMOFLIPID is a brand of lipid emulsion specifically designed for parenteral nutrition. It is formulated as a 20% lipid emulsion that combines soybean oil, medium-chain triglycerides, olive oil, and fish oil, creating a balanced mixture aimed at providing a more physiological composition for nutritional support. This fat emulsion is particularly beneficial for intravenous nutrition in newborns, as it supplies essential fatty acids and calories necessary for their growth and development. Notably, SMOFLIPID is recognized for its high concentration of alpha-tocopherol and is rich in docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) and eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA), which are important components for overall health."}{"title": "GLICEROFOSFATO S\u00d3DICO:Sodium glycerophosphate is a compound used to prevent precipitation of calcium-phosphate salts in parenteral nutrition"}{"title": "MOLIBDENO:MOLIBDENO, or molybdenum, is a trace element that serves as a cofactor for various enzymes involved in the metabolism of pyrimidines and purines. It is found in foods such as milk and legumes. Molybdenum is essential for health, but deficiencies can occur, particularly in patients with inflammatory bowel disease, where it may contribute to health complications. Additionally, in pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition, the intake of molybdenum should be limited in cases of renal insufficiency. Overall, molybdenum plays a significant role in enzyme function, and specific dietary recommendations are advised to ensure adequate intake while avoiding potential excesses in vulnerable populations."}{"title": "IODO:Iodine is a trace element essential for thyroid hormone production, with specific dosage recommendations for pediatric patients"}{"title": "AMINOVEN INFANT\u00ae:Aminoven Infant\u00ae is a pediatric amino acid solution specifically designed for the nutritional therapy of infants. It contains a carefully formulated blend of amino acids that supports the nutritional needs of infants up to 1 year old. This product is essential for providing the necessary nutrients to promote healthy growth and development in young children."}{"title": "AMINOPLASMAL L-10\u00ae:Aminoplasmal L-10\u00ae is a nutritional product recommended for children older than 1 year."}{"title": "AMINOSTERIL-N HEPA\u00ae:Aminosteril-N Hepa\u00ae is a solution of amino acids indicated for patients with hepatic insufficiency and encephalopathy."}{"title": "NEPHRO-TECT\u00ae:Nephro-tect\u00ae is a nutritional solution indicated for patients with renal insufficiency and anuria."}{"title": "PEDITRACE\u00ae:Peditrace\u00ae is a nutritional supplement containing trace elements for pediatric patients."}{"title": "INFUVITE\u00ae:INFUVITE\u00ae is a vitamin composition used in pediatric nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRICIONES ESTANDARIZADAS:Standardized nutrition refers to specific nutritional formulations for patients requiring prolonged fasting."}{"title": "AMINOACIDOS:Amino acids are essential nutrients that play a crucial role in protein synthesis and growth, particularly in infants who are receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HEPARINA:Heparina is an anticoagulant medication primarily used to prevent and treat blood clots, particularly in patients at risk of thromboembolic events such as deep vein thrombosis. It is often utilized in medical settings, especially in conjunction with intravenous nutrition administration. Heparina is sometimes included in parenteral nutrition solutions, although its use is not routine due to potential risks associated with mixing. \n\nIn particular, Heparina is employed to prolong the use of catheters and to mitigate complications related to catheter obstruction and sepsis. It may also be used alongside taurolidine in parenteral nutrition to prevent clotting. Specifically, Heparina can be administered via central lines at a concentration of 0.5 UI/ml, highlighting its importance in managing catheter-related complications. Overall, Heparina plays a crucial role in enhancing patient safety and efficacy in various medical treatments involving intravenous and parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "PEDI\u00c1TRICAS:Pedi\u00e1tricas refers to the pediatric formulations and nutritional contributions for children of various weights."}{"title": "SOLUTION FORMULATIONS:Solution formulations are medical mixtures that include various components like electrolytes, vitamins, and glucose for patient care."}{"title": "CALORIC COMPONENTS:Caloric components are the nutritional values derived from carbohydrates, proteins, and lipids, calculated for patient dietary needs."}{"title": "M. GORMAZ MORENO:M. Gormaz Moreno is an author who has made significant contributions to the field of neonatal nutrition. They are involved in writing a chapter on enteral nutrition for newborns in a medical text, as well as contributing to a chapter on neonatal parenteral nutrition. Through these contributions, M. Gormaz Moreno plays a vital role in advancing knowledge and practices related to the nutritional care of newborns."}{"title": "J. DALMAU SERRA:J. Dalmau Serra is an accomplished author who has made significant contributions to the field of pediatric nutrition. He is notably involved in writing chapters on enteral nutrition for newborns and neonatal parenteral nutrition in a medical text, showcasing his expertise in these critical areas of infant care. Additionally, J. Dalmau Serra addresses complications associated with long-term central venous catheters in pediatrics, further highlighting his commitment to improving health outcomes for children. Through these contributions, he plays a vital role in advancing knowledge and practices in pediatric nutrition and care."}{"title": "ACADEMIA AMERICANA DE PEDIATR\u00cdA:The Academia Americana de Pediatr\u00eda (AAP) is a professional association of pediatricians dedicated to the health and well-being of infants, children, adolescents, and young adults."}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA DE PEDIATR\u00cdA:The Asociaci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola de Pediatr\u00eda (AEP) is a professional organization dedicated to promoting the health and welfare of children in Spain. It focuses on various aspects of pediatric health, including nutrition, and provides dietary recommendations for children. Among its initiatives, the AEP emphasizes the importance of vitamin D intake guidelines to ensure the well-being of children. Through its efforts, the AEP plays a crucial role in advocating for and supporting the health needs of the pediatric population in Spain."}{"title": "GASTROENTERITIS:Gastroenteritis is an inflammation of the stomach and intestines, often resulting in vomiting and diarrhea, which can be reduced by breastfeeding."}{"title": "INFECCI\u00d3N RESPIRATORIA:Infecci\u00f3n respiratoria refers to respiratory infections that can be lessened in incidence through breastfeeding."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD CEL\u00cdACA:Celiac disease, known as \"enfermedad cel\u00edaca,\" is an autoimmune disorder characterized by the body's adverse reaction to gluten, a protein found in grains such as wheat, barley, rye, and oats. The ingestion of gluten leads to damage in the small intestine, resulting in malabsorption of essential nutrients, including vitamins and minerals such as vitamin E and magnesium. This malabsorption can contribute to various health issues, including an increased risk of kidney stones and potential growth delays in affected individuals.\n\nCeliac disease is also included in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases, highlighting its complexity and the need for careful medical evaluation. Interestingly, some studies suggest that the incidence of celiac disease may be lower in breastfed infants, indicating a potential protective effect of breastfeeding against the development of this condition. Overall, celiac disease is a significant health concern that requires strict adherence to a gluten-free diet to manage symptoms and prevent complications."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE MUERTE S\u00daBITA DEL LACTANTE:S\u00edndrome de muerte s\u00fabita del lactante (SIDS) is the sudden unexplained death of an infant, which has been associated with breastfeeding practices."}{"title": "HIPERTENSI\u00d3N:HIPERTENSI\u00d3N is a medical condition characterized by consistently elevated blood pressure, which can lead to various health complications. It is defined as a condition in which the force of the blood against the artery walls is too high. This chronic condition is often associated with several health issues, including kidney stones and cardiometabolic disorders, and may also be linked to renal insufficiency. \n\nThere are different types of hypertension, including hipertensi\u00f3n de origen endocrinol\u00f3gico, which refers to hypertension caused by endocrine disorders. The condition can be influenced by dietary factors, particularly sodium intake, as increased salt consumption has been linked to elevated blood pressure levels. \n\nIn some cases, hypertension can be severe and resistant to treatment, necessitating specific dietary considerations. Additionally, it has been noted that breastfeeding may be associated with a lower risk of developing hypertension. Overall, HIPERTENSI\u00d3N is a significant health concern that requires careful management and monitoring in patients, as it is often part of their medical history."}{"title": "DIABETES TIPO I Y II:Diabetes tipo I y II are forms of diabetes that may have a reduced risk in individuals who were breastfed as infants."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR:\"Enfermedad cardiovascular\" refers to a group of medical conditions that affect the heart and blood vessels. This term encompasses a wide range of disorders, including those linked to dyslipidemia, obesity, diabetes, metabolic syndrome, and hypertension. The European Society of Cardiology emphasizes the importance of managing risk factors associated with cardiovascular disease, which is a significant health issue globally.\n\nCardiovascular disease is often influenced by dietary habits, particularly the intake of trans fatty acids and saturated fats, as well as lifestyle factors. It is also associated with metabolic disorders such as hyperuricemia and can contribute to complications in patients with diabetes, leading to increased morbidity and mortality. Additionally, there is evidence suggesting that breastfeeding may reduce the prevalence of certain cardiovascular conditions.\n\nThe condition is also linked to renal issues, such as kidney stones, and is a risk factor for familial combined hyperlipidemia. Overall, \"enfermedad cardiovascular\" represents a critical area of concern in public health, necessitating careful monitoring and management to mitigate its impact on individuals' health."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE MAMA:C\u00e1ncer de mama, or breast cancer, is a prevalent malignancy that originates in the cells of the breasts. It is influenced by various risk factors, including hormonal treatments, dietary habits, and genetic predispositions. Women with MEN1 syndrome are at a higher risk of developing breast cancer at younger ages compared to the general population. \n\nDietary factors play a significant role in the risk of developing breast cancer. Increased consumption of fruits and vegetables, particularly cruciferous vegetables, has been associated with a reduced risk. Additionally, higher soy intake, due to the presence of isoflavones that act as natural modulators of estrogen receptors, may also lower the risk. Conversely, a higher intake of red and processed meats has been positively correlated with an increased risk of breast cancer, although some studies have not found this relationship to be significant.\n\nNutritional deficiencies, particularly in vitamin E and vitamin C, may influence breast cancer risk, with suggestions that a daily intake of 300 mg of vitamin C could decrease the risk. Furthermore, dietary fiber intake has been linked to a lower risk of breast cancer, indicating that an increase in fiber consumption may be beneficial.\n\nObesity, especially in postmenopausal women, is another factor that can elevate the risk of breast cancer. Breastfeeding has been shown to correlate with a lower incidence of the disease. Additionally, breast cancer can lead to complications such as hypercalcemia, particularly in advanced stages of the disease.\n\nResearch has also explored the potential protective effects of omega-3 fatty acids, suggesting that supplementation may reduce breast cancer risk. Overall, C\u00e1ncer de mama is a complex condition influenced by a combination of genetic, hormonal, and dietary factors, necessitating careful monitoring and lifestyle considerations for at-risk populations."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE OVARIO:C\u00e1ncer de ovario, or ovarian cancer, is a type of cancer that has been extensively studied in relation to various dietary factors. Research indicates that obesity is a significant risk factor for the development of this cancer. Additionally, there is evidence suggesting that breastfeeding may be associated with a reduced risk of ovarian cancer. \n\nDietary habits also play a role in the risk of developing this disease. Specifically, a high consumption of dairy products, defined as more than four servings per day, has been linked to an increased risk of ovarian cancer. Conversely, there appears to be no association between the consumption of red or processed meat and the incidence of ovarian cancer; however, the presence of nitrites in processed meats may elevate the risk. \n\nOverall, C\u00e1ncer de ovario is influenced by a complex interplay of dietary factors, obesity, and reproductive history, highlighting the importance of lifestyle choices in its prevention and management."}{"title": "IHAN:The Initiative for the Promotion of Breastfeeding (IHAN) is an organization that promotes breastfeeding practices in hospitals and healthcare settings."}{"title": "UNICEF:The United Nations Children's Fund (UNICEF), also known as the United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund, is an agency dedicated to providing humanitarian and developmental aid to children around the globe. UNICEF focuses on improving the lives of children and their families, addressing critical issues such as child mortality, particularly in relation to health challenges like diarrhea. The agency advocates for interventions such as zinc supplementation in cases of acute diarrhea, highlighting its commitment to enhancing child health and well-being. Through its various initiatives, UNICEF aims to ensure that every child has the opportunity to thrive and reach their full potential."}{"title": "LACTANCIA MATERNA:LACTANCIA MATERNA, or breastfeeding, is the process of feeding a baby with milk from the mother's breast. This practice is highly recommended for infants, particularly during the first six months of life, as it provides adequate nutrition and covers their iron needs, despite the milk's low iron content. Breastfeeding offers numerous health benefits for both the mother and the child, making it an essential aspect of infant care and development."}{"title": "GALACTOSEMIA:GALACTOSEMIA is a genetic metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to process galactose, a sugar found in milk. This condition requires special dietary considerations, particularly for infants, as it can lead to various health complications if not managed properly. Individuals with galactosemia must adhere to strict dietary restrictions and management strategies to avoid the adverse effects associated with the disorder. The inability to metabolize galactose can result in a range of clinical symptoms and complications, underscoring the importance of proper treatment and dietary management for those affected by this condition."}{"title": "HIV:HIV, or Human Immunodeficiency Virus, is a viral infection that primarily targets the immune system, leading to a range of health complications. One of the rare complications associated with HIV is adrenal insufficiency. The virus can be transmitted from mother to child during breastfeeding, highlighting the importance of understanding its transmission routes. Additionally, individuals infected with HIV may experience increased cardiovascular risk and menopausal symptoms, particularly in women. Overall, HIV poses significant challenges to health, necessitating awareness and management of its various effects on the body."}{"title": "BRUCELLOSIS:Brucellosis is an infectious disease caused by bacteria that can be transmitted through unpasteurized milk and can affect breastfeeding."}{"title": "TUBERCULOSIS:Tuberculosis is an infectious bacterial disease that primarily affects the lungs but can also lead to serious complications in other parts of the body. It is particularly concerning in low-income countries, where it can result in adrenal insufficiency due to the destruction of the adrenal glands. This condition, known as primary adrenal insufficiency, can arise as a complication of the disease. Additionally, untreated tuberculosis poses risks to breastfeeding, potentially affecting both the mother and the infant. Other complications associated with tuberculosis include ascites quilosa, which is the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the abdominal cavity. Overall, tuberculosis is a significant health issue that can lead to various severe health outcomes if not properly managed."}{"title": "CES\u00c1REA:Ces\u00e1rea, or cesarean section, is a surgical procedure employed to deliver a baby through incisions made in the abdomen and uterus. This method of delivery can have implications for breastfeeding initiation, potentially affecting the early stages of breastfeeding for the newborn. Additionally, ces\u00e1rea is associated with a distinct microbiota composition in newborns, which is characterized by the presence of skin-related microorganisms. This difference in microbiota may have further implications for the health and development of infants born via cesarean section."}{"title": "LECHE MATERNA:LECHE MATERNA, or breast milk, is the milk produced by a mother to feed her infant, providing essential nutrients and antibodies crucial for the infant's health. It is recommended for feeding infants whenever possible, as it serves as the natural food for newborns. Breast milk is particularly important for premature infants, aiding in their nutritional needs and helping with intestinal adaptation. It is considered the optimal nutrition for newborns, promoting self-regulation in feeding practices. Additionally, LECHE MATERNA contains vital components such as iodine and other essential vitamins, making it a key element in infant nutrition. The composition and significance of breast milk have been extensively analyzed, underscoring its importance in supporting the health and development of infants."}{"title": "DIABETES TIPO II:Type II diabetes is a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and can be influenced by breastfeeding."}{"title": "ARTRITIS REUMATOIDE:Artritis Reumatoide es una enfermedad autoinmune que se caracteriza por la inflamaci\u00f3n cr\u00f3nica de las articulaciones. Esta condici\u00f3n puede estar relacionada con niveles elevados de cobre en el organismo. Adem\u00e1s, se ha observado que la artritis reumatoide puede beneficiarse de la salud proporcionada por la lactancia materna. Es importante destacar que esta enfermedad autoinmune tambi\u00e9n puede coexistir con otros trastornos autoinmunes, como la diabetes mellitus tipo 1."}{"title": "V\u00cdNCULO AFECTIVO:The emotional bond established between a mother and her child, which can be enhanced through breastfeeding."}{"title": "CHUPETE:A pacifier, which is sometimes used by parents, can affect breastfeeding practices and is discussed in the context of breastfeeding recommendations."}{"title": "GRUPOS DE APOYO A LA LACTANCIA:Support groups for breastfeeding mothers that provide assistance and encouragement for successful breastfeeding practices."}{"title": "R. SCHANLER:R. Schanler is an author who contributed to the work on the nutrition of preterm infants, specifically discussing human milk composition and guidelines for infant nutrition."}{"title": "HUMAN MILK:Human milk is discussed in the context of its composition and nutritional value for preterm infants, as well as guidelines for its use."}{"title": "TSANG R.:Tsang R. is the editor of the book \"Nutrition of the Preterm Infant,\" which includes a chapter on human milk."}{"title": "DIGITAL EDUCATIONAL PUBLISHING, INC.:Digital Educational Publishing, INC. is the publisher of the book that contains information on human milk and infant nutrition."}{"title": "PRETERM INFANT:A preterm infant is a baby born before the 37th week of pregnancy, who may require special nutritional considerations, including the composition of human milk."}{"title": "COMPOSICI\u00d3N DE LA LECHE MATERNA:Composici\u00f3n de la leche materna refers to the detailed analysis of the nutritional components of breast milk, including energy, proteins, fats, and carbohydrates."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS Y VITAMINAS:Suplementos y vitaminas refers to the guidelines and recommendations for administering supplements and vitamins to infants, particularly in cases of excessive weight loss or dehydration."}{"title": "INGESTA:Ingesta refers to the intake of food or nutrients by the infant, which is monitored to ensure adequate nutrition and growth."}{"title": "P\u00c9RDIDA PONDERAL:P\u00e9rdida ponderal refers to the weight loss experienced by infants after birth, which is a critical factor in assessing their health and nutritional needs. Additionally, weight loss is a primary goal in the treatment of obesity, often requiring individualized strategies based on patient needs. This highlights the importance of understanding weight loss in different contexts, such as in newborns for health assessment and in adults for obesity management."}{"title": "LECHE DE MADRES DE PRET\u00c9RMINO:"}{"title": "COMIT\u00c9 DE NUTRICI\u00d3N DE LA AEP:The Committee on Nutrition of the AEP provides recommendations for infant nutrition and supplementation, particularly regarding vitamin K and vitamin D for newborns."}{"title": "ESPGHAN:ESPGHAN, the European Society for Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition, is an organization dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations on pediatric nutrition, particularly focusing on infants and children. It plays a crucial role in developing guidelines for pediatric parenteral nutrition, especially for vulnerable populations such as infants and newborns. Additionally, ESPGHAN is recognized for its contributions to the field through the publication of position papers, including those addressing intestinal failure and transplantation. The organization has also published specific recommendations regarding the composition of infant formulas, with notable guidelines released in 2005. Overall, ESPGHAN serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals involved in the nutritional care of children, ensuring that best practices are followed in pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition."}{"title": "LACTANCIA ARTIFICIAL:Artificial lactation refers to the use of industrially prepared formulas for infants when breastfeeding is not an option."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS ADAPTADAS:F\u00d3RMULAS ADAPTADAS are specialized nutritional products designed for infants who have allergies to cow's milk proteins. These adapted formulas serve as specially prepared milk substitutes for infants when breastfeeding is not possible or is contraindicated. They provide essential nutrients tailored to meet the dietary needs of sensitive infants, ensuring their health and growth in situations where traditional milk options are unsuitable."}{"title": "EUROPEAN REGULATION:The European regulation oversees the preparation of infant formulas, ensuring they meet nutritional needs for infants during their first six months of life."}{"title": "LACTOSE:Lactose is a sugar found in milk and dairy products, serving as the primary carbohydrate in infant formulas, which is essential for energy and growth in infants. While it is allowed in the diets of patients with certain glycogen storage diseases, it can also cause intolerance in some individuals, particularly those with celiac disease. For patients with lactose intolerance, lactose may need to be substituted with lactose-free options, and it is often excluded from formulas designed for infants with specific allergies or intolerances."}{"title": "PRETERM NEWBORN:Preterm newborns have increased nutritional needs compared to term newborns and are at risk of extrauterine malnutrition."}{"title": "MOTHER:Mothers play a crucial role in the early stages of a child's life, as they are advised to receive information on the proper preparation of infant formulas and the nutritional needs of their newborns. During pregnancy, mothers undergo significant physiological changes to support fetal development, ensuring the health and well-being of their unborn child. Additionally, in specific cases, such as that of a patient with a genetic condition, the mother may also be a carrier of genetic mutations, like the A243G mutation, and may face her own health challenges, including diabetes and hearing loss. This highlights the multifaceted responsibilities and health considerations that mothers navigate throughout pregnancy and beyond."}{"title": "NECROTIZING ENTEROCOLITIS:Necrotizing enterocolitis (NEC) is a serious gastrointestinal condition that can affect preterm newborns, with a relationship to feeding practices."}{"title": "BREAST MILK:Breast milk provides numerous benefits to preterm newborns, including reduced mortality and lower rates of infections."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL GUIDELINES:Nutritional guidelines are comprehensive recommendations designed to assist individuals and healthcare professionals in making informed dietary choices to promote health and prevent chronic diseases. These guidelines are particularly important in managing dietary intake for specific populations, such as renal patients and individuals with liver disease, ensuring that their unique nutritional needs are met. Additionally, nutritional guidelines aim to prevent nutritional deficiencies and support health outcomes in vulnerable populations, including preterm newborns who require adequate nutrition for growth. Overall, these guidelines serve as a crucial tool in both clinical settings and general health promotion, advocating for proper dietary practices that contribute to overall well-being."}{"title": "INFANT FORMULAS:Infant formulas are specialized food products designed to meet the nutritional needs of infants, especially those who are not breastfed."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL EMERGENCY:Nutritional emergency refers to the critical situation where preterm newborns require immediate nutritional support to prevent malnutrition."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL NEEDS:Nutritional needs encompass the dietary requirements essential for maintaining health across various populations. This includes the specific needs of older adults, who require adequate trace elements and vitamins to support their well-being. Additionally, nutritional needs vary significantly for preterm infants, whose dietary requirements differ from those of full-term newborns, necessitating careful consideration and tailored nutrition plans. Furthermore, for patients undergoing nutritional support, particularly in critical care settings, it is crucial to calculate and meet their specific dietary requirements to ensure optimal recovery and health outcomes. Overall, nutritional needs are diverse and must be addressed according to the unique requirements of different groups."}{"title": "LECHE MATERNA DONADA:Donated human milk (LMD) is recognized as a second option when maternal milk is unavailable, used under specific medical indications."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS DE PREMATUROS:Formulas designed for premature infants to meet their nutritional needs, providing higher calories, proteins, and minerals."}{"title": "ALPREM CLINIC 1:A hospital-use formula specifically designed for premature newborns weighing less than 1,800 grams, with higher protein content."}{"title": "ESPGHAN 2010:The ESPGHAN 2010 guidelines provide nutritional recommendations for the enteral feeding of premature newborns."}{"title": "RECI\u00c9N NACIDOS PRET\u00c9RMINO:\"Reci\u00e9n nacidos pret\u00e9rmino\" refers to premature newborns who are born before the completion of 37 weeks of gestation. These infants often have low birth weight and specific developmental needs, which necessitate specialized nutritional support. Due to their early arrival, preterm newborns may require immediate nutritional intervention to prevent adverse effects associated with fasting and to support their growth and development."}{"title": "LACANTIA:Lactation is the process of feeding infants with breast milk, which is particularly important for premature infants to receive essential nutrients and antibodies."}{"title": "MATERIALES DE LA LECHE MATERNA:The composition of human milk varies significantly, impacting the nutritional intake of premature infants."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES EN LA ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:Feeding difficulties in premature infants can arise from various factors, including the availability of maternal milk and the infant's ability to tolerate feeding volumes."}{"title": "RETINOPAT\u00cdA DE LA PREMATURIDAD:"}{"title": "JOURNAL OF PEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY AND NUTRITION:The Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research and commentary focused on pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition. It serves as a platform for disseminating research findings and guidelines that pertain to pediatric nutrition and gastrointestinal health, contributing to the advancement of knowledge in these critical areas of child health."}{"title": "PRETERM INFANTS:Preterm infants are defined as babies born before the completion of 37 weeks of gestation. Due to their early birth, they often require specialized medical care and have specific nutritional needs that differ from those of full-term infants. These infants necessitate specialized nutritional guidelines and formulas to support their development and ensure they receive the appropriate care for their unique circumstances."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL M\u00cdNIMA O TR\u00d3FICA:A feeding protocol aimed at stimulating and nourishing the immature intestines of preterm infants."}{"title": "NEC:NEC refers to necrotizing enterocolitis, a serious gastrointestinal condition that can affect premature infants. This clinical guideline or protocol is focused on the dietary needs and management of these vulnerable infants, emphasizing the importance of proper nutrition to mitigate the risks associated with this condition."}{"title": "RCIU:RCIU, or Retraso de Crecimiento Intrauterino, refers to a condition characterized by intrauterine growth restriction, where a fetus fails to achieve normal weight during pregnancy. This condition is defined as being small for gestational age at birth and indicates that the fetus does not reach its genetic growth potential while in utero."}{"title": "DHA:DHA, or Docosahexaenoic Acid, is an essential omega-3 fatty acid that plays a critical role in human health, particularly in brain and heart function. It is vital for cognitive development and is a significant component of the brain's structure, contributing to brain health and cognitive function. DHA is also important for cardiovascular health and may help prevent progressive atrophy of the cerebral cortex, thereby reducing the risk of Alzheimer's disease.\n\nIn addition to its neurological benefits, DHA is proposed for dietary supplementation in conditions such as cystic fibrosis to help modulate inflammatory responses and improve immune function. It is derived from alpha-linolenic acid (ALA) and is crucial for eye function as well. Furthermore, recent European legislation emphasizes the necessity of including DHA in infant formulas, highlighting its importance for brain development in preterm infants. Overall, DHA is recognized as a vital nutrient for maintaining overall health and well-being."}{"title": "AA:Arachidonic acid, an essential fatty acid important for growth and development in preterm infants."}{"title": "CA:Calcium, an essential mineral for bone development in preterm infants."}{"title": "P:Phosphorus (P) is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in bone health and energy metabolism, particularly in preterm infants. It is important to monitor phosphorus levels in patients at risk of refeeding syndrome to prevent metabolic complications."}{"title": "RATIO CA/P:The ratio of calcium to phosphorus, which is important for the nutritional balance in preterm infants."}{"title": "IBUPROFENO:Ibuprofen is a medication mentioned in the context of treatment for certain conditions in premature infants."}{"title": "RN:RN refers to a registered nurse who plays a crucial role in the care and management of premature infants. This specialized nursing professional is involved in providing essential support to neonatal patients, particularly those who require specialized nutritional assistance through parenteral nutrition due to their inability to feed orally. The RN's expertise is vital in ensuring the health and well-being of these vulnerable infants."}{"title": "RNPT:RNPT refers to \"Reci\u00e9n Nacidos Prematuros\" or \"Premature Newborns,\" a specific group of patients that includes preterm newborns who require specialized nutritional support due to their unique health needs. This group encompasses newborns with low birth weight and very low birth weight, who are particularly susceptible to conditions such as hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia. As a result, they require careful nutritional management, including elevated glucose intake to prevent hypoglycemia and adherence to specific nutritional guidelines when receiving parenteral nutrition. Additionally, RNPT can also refer to a registered nurse specializing in the care of these premature infants, ensuring they receive the necessary attention and support for optimal growth and development."}{"title": "FORTIFICACI\u00d3N DE LA LECHE MATERNA:Fortification of breast milk is a process designed to enhance the nutritional content of breast milk for premature infants."}{"title": "ECN:ECN refers to enterocolitis necrotizing, a serious gastrointestinal condition that can affect premature infants."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N ENTERAL:Alimentaci\u00f3n enteral is a method of providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract, primarily utilized when patients are stabilized. This approach is particularly significant for infants, especially those who are premature, as it ensures they receive essential nutrients directly through their digestive system. Alimentaci\u00f3n enteral serves as an alternative to parenteral nutrition, offering a means to deliver nutrition effectively through the digestive tract."}{"title": "SOG:SOG refers to the method of administration for feeding, specifically through a gastric tube."}{"title": "GCI:GCI refers to a method of feeding that involves administering nutrition over a set period, typically used for infants."}{"title": "DISTENSI\u00d3N ABDOMINAL:Distensi\u00f3n abdominal is a clinical sign that may indicate feeding intolerance in infants. It is also recognized as a gastrointestinal symptom that can arise from the use of certain medications in conjunction with enteral nutrition. This condition highlights the importance of monitoring abdominal distension, particularly in vulnerable populations such as infants, as it may signal underlying issues related to their nutritional intake and medication effects."}{"title": "DOLOR A LA PALPACI\u00d3N:Dolor a la palpaci\u00f3n is a clinical sign that may suggest gastrointestinal issues in infants."}{"title": "PERISTALTISMO:Peristaltismo refers to the movement of the intestines, which can be assessed to evaluate feeding tolerance in infants."}{"title": "RECI\u00c9N NACIDOS PREMATUROS:\"RECI\u00c9N NACIDOS PREMATUROS\" refers to newborns who are born before 37 weeks of gestation. These infants require special attention in terms of their feeding and care due to their physiological immaturity. They are at risk of undernutrition and therefore need specific nutritional support to ensure their health and development."}{"title": "MEAD-JOHNSON:Mead-Johnson is a company that specializes in pediatric nutrition, focusing on the development and production of products designed for infant feeding. One of their notable products is Enfalac HMF, which is specifically formulated to meet the nutritional needs of infants."}{"title": "HIDROPOLIVIT:Hidropolivit is a liquid multivitamin supplement designed to enhance hydration and nutrient intake. It is particularly recommended for premature infants to ensure they receive adequate vitamin D, which is crucial for their development. Additionally, Hidropolivit serves as a polivitaminic supplement that provides essential vitamins and minerals necessary for the growth and health of infants and children."}{"title": "DHA VIT:DHA Vit is a nutritional supplement designed to support the health and nutritional needs of infants. It contains DHA, along with vitamins A, D, and E, which are essential for the proper development and well-being of young children."}{"title": "TABLE 5:Table 5 serves multiple purposes related to dietary management in a pediatric hospital setting. It presents dietary recommendations for liquid intake based on the age of pediatric patients, ensuring that their hydration needs are appropriately met. Additionally, Table 5 details the composition of available milk fortifiers within the hospital, providing essential information about their nutritional content to support the dietary needs of infants and children. Furthermore, it includes information on dietary restrictions for patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD), specifically focusing on the limitations regarding leucine content to manage this metabolic condition effectively. Overall, Table 5 is a comprehensive resource for dietary guidelines and nutritional support for pediatric patients."}{"title": "TABLE 3A:Table 3A outlines the vitamin and mineral requirements for premature infants."}{"title": "TABLE 3B:Table 3B provides additional information on the vitamin and mineral requirements for premature infants."}{"title": "PHOSPHORUS:Phosphorus is a vital mineral that plays a critical role in bone health and energy production. It is particularly important for various age groups, with specific dietary reference intake levels outlined in dietary guidelines. The mineral is essential for maintaining calcium homeostasis and is often studied in relation to chronic kidney disease (CKD) and dietary management.\n\nIn the context of dietary intake, phosphorus is significant for premature infants, as it supports their bone health and overall development. However, for patients with chronic kidney disease, phosphorus intake must be carefully managed. High levels of phosphorus can lead to nutritional deficits and bone disease, necessitating dietary restrictions to prevent complications. For individuals undergoing dialysis, the recommended phosphorus intake is approximately 17 mg/kg/day.\n\nOverall, phosphorus is a crucial dietary mineral that must be balanced to support health, particularly in vulnerable populations such as infants and patients with renal insufficiency."}{"title": "VITAMIN D:Vitamin D is a crucial fat-soluble vitamin that plays a significant role in maintaining bone health and muscle function. It is essential for calcium absorption, which is vital for bone integrity, and has been linked to various health outcomes, including the risk of cancer, cardiovascular disease, and frailty. Vitamin D deficiency is a common concern, particularly in specific populations such as patients with anorexia nervosa, liver disease, and those who have undergone bariatric surgery, as well as in older adults and preterm infants. \n\nResearch indicates that optimizing Vitamin D levels is important for preventing metabolic bone disease and supporting overall health. It is often recommended for supplementation in individuals at risk of osteoporosis and is particularly relevant for maintaining muscle health in older adults, potentially aiding in the treatment of sarcopenia. Additionally, Vitamin D deficiency has been associated with the development of food allergies and is common in patients with conditions like EPOC and BQ.\n\nDosage recommendations for Vitamin D are typically based on individual factors such as calcium, phosphorus, and parathyroid hormone (PTH) levels, with a general guideline to maintain 25OH-vitamin D levels above 30 ng/dl. The importance of adequate Vitamin D intake is emphasized across various health contexts, including its role in immune function and fall prevention in older adults. Overall, Vitamin D is recognized as a vital nutrient that supports bone health and has implications for a wide range of health outcomes."}{"title": "PREMATURIDAD:Prematuridad is the condition of being born before the full term of pregnancy, often leading to various health challenges. This condition, known as prematurity, significantly impacts the nutritional needs of the infant, necessitating specific supplementation to support their development and health."}{"title": "CALCIUM:Calcium is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in maintaining bone health and is vital for the development of strong bones and teeth, particularly in children and preterm infants. Its importance extends to various age groups, with specific intake recommendations outlined in dietary guidelines. Calcium is also significant in the context of osteoporosis management, as it is often supplemented to aid in bone density recovery, especially in patients with conditions such as Anorexia Nervosa or those undergoing dialysis, where a daily intake of 1-1.5 g is recommended.\n\nIn addition to its role in bone health, calcium is involved in several biological processes, including the regulation of homeostasis in the body and the signaling process that triggers insulin secretion from \u03b2-cells. Research has explored the relationship between calcium intake and cancer risk, as well as its potential inverse relationship with blood pressure, particularly in individuals sensitive to salt.\n\nHowever, calcium's metabolism can be affected by various factors, such as gastric resection, which may decrease its absorption and lead to secondary hyperparathyroidism and increased bone resorption. Furthermore, while calcium is vital for health, excessive intake can contribute to the formation of kidney stones, particularly calcium oxalate stones, and its excretion is influenced by dietary factors.\n\nCalcium is predominantly found in dairy products and leafy greens, making it an important nutrient in diets aimed at preventing osteoporosis and promoting overall cardiovascular function. Overall, calcium is a vital micronutrient that supports numerous physiological functions and is essential for maintaining optimal health."}{"title": "EPO:EPO refers to erythropoietin, a hormone that stimulates red blood cell production, often used in medical treatments for infants."}{"title": "INFATRINI:Infatrini is a high-calorie, semi-elemental nutritional formula produced by Nutricia, specifically designed for infants up to 12 months of age who have increased energy needs. This polymeric formula provides 1 kcal/ml, making it suitable for infants requiring nutritional support to promote their growth and development. Infatrini aims to meet the unique dietary requirements of young children, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for healthy growth."}{"title": "DISPLASIA BRONCOPULMONAR:Bronchopulmonary dysplasia, also known as displasia broncopulmonar, is a serious chronic lung condition that primarily affects premature infants. This condition necessitates specialized care and management due to its complexity. Additionally, it requires careful dietary considerations to support the health and development of affected infants."}{"title": "CARDIOPAT\u00cdA CONG\u00c9NITA:Congenital heart disease refers to a range of heart defects present at birth, which may require specialized nutritional support."}{"title": "VITAMIN B2:Vitamin B2, also known as riboflavin, is a vital B vitamin that plays a crucial role in energy production and cellular function. It is commonly included in dietary supplements, such as Hidropolivit, highlighting its importance in maintaining overall health and supporting metabolic processes."}{"title": "VITAMIN PP:Vitamin PP, also known as niacin, is important for metabolism and is part of the composition of Hidropolivit."}{"title": "VITAMIN B6:Vitamin B6, also known as pyridoxine, is a vital nutrient that plays a significant role in various metabolic processes. It serves as a cofactor for enzymes involved in amino acid metabolism, particularly in the conversion of homocysteine to cystathionine. This vitamin is essential for protein metabolism and cognitive development. Additionally, Vitamin B6 is involved in oxalate metabolism, and its deficiency can lead to increased oxalate production.\n\nResearch has explored the potential role of Vitamin B6 in managing metabolic disorders, although findings have been inconclusive for certain conditions such as Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI). For patients undergoing dialysis, it is recommended to take Vitamin B6 in doses of 10-20 mg per day to support their health. Vitamin B6 can be found in various supplements, including products like Hidropolivit, highlighting its importance in dietary intake."}{"title": "VITAMIN H:Vitamin H, also known as biotin, is important for fatty acid synthesis and is included in nutritional supplements."}{"title": "VITAMIN C:Vitamin C is a vital water-soluble nutrient known for its essential roles in immune function, skin health, and collagen formation. It is present in various supplements, such as Hidropolivit, and is recognized for its antioxidant properties, which may help prevent the formation of free radicals and reduce oxidative damage in cells. While Vitamin C is important for overall health, its intake should be carefully managed in certain populations. For instance, it is recommended that patients with iron overload limit their Vitamin C intake, as excessive amounts can increase iron absorption. Additionally, patients undergoing dialysis are advised to take doses of less than 150 mg per day. Furthermore, Vitamin C supplementation has been associated with increased urinary oxalate excretion due to its metabolism to oxalate. Overall, Vitamin C is an essential nutrient that supports various bodily functions, but its supplementation should be approached with caution in specific health conditions."}{"title": "VITAMIN E:Vitamin E is a fat-soluble antioxidant that plays a crucial role in protecting cells from damage and supporting immune function. It is known for its ability to protect cell membranes from oxidative damage, which may contribute to a reduced incidence of Alzheimer's disease. Vitamin E is commonly found in dietary supplements, such as those containing DHA, and is recommended in specific dosages for patients with certain conditions, including those with hereditary hemochromatosis, where its levels are often decreased. Supplementation in these cases may help alleviate oxidative stress, further underscoring the importance of Vitamin E in maintaining cellular health."}{"title": "IRON:Iron is a vital micronutrient essential for the production of hemoglobin, playing a crucial role in overall health, particularly in infants, toddlers, and women of childbearing age. Its dietary reference intake varies across different age groups, as outlined in dietary guidelines. Iron deficiency and resulting anemia are common, especially after bariatric surgery, necessitating supplementation to prevent these issues. This is particularly important for patients receiving erythropoietin, as iron supplementation is often required to address anemia in these cases, including during dialysis treatment.\n\nIron is frequently included in infant formulas and supplements, although its addition can be controversial, especially for preterm infants. It is important to note that while iron is essential for health, excessive intake can lead to oxidative stress and neurodegeneration. Additionally, certain dietary components, such as corn starch, can interfere with iron absorption, highlighting the need for careful management of iron intake to meet the recommended dietary allowance (RDA) and prevent deficiencies in vulnerable populations."}{"title": "DEXTRINOMALTOSE:Dextrinomaltose is a carbohydrate used as a source of energy in nutritional supplements and infant formulas."}{"title": "VITAMIN A:Vitamin A is a fat-soluble vitamin that is essential for various bodily functions, including vision, immune function, and skin health. It is particularly important for patients with specific health conditions, as there are recommended dosages tailored for their needs. Additionally, Vitamin A contributes to the growth and development of the skeleton by influencing protein synthesis and the differentiation of bone cells."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA PARA PREMATUROS:F\u00f3rmula para Prematuros is a specialized formula designed to meet the higher energy needs of premature infants."}{"title": "CARRASCOSA:Carrascosa is referenced for providing growth charts suitable for the Spanish population, particularly for assessing newborns."}{"title": "FENTON:Fenton is referenced for providing growth charts that include children up to 52 weeks postconceptional age."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N OPTIMA:Nutrici\u00f3n \u00f3ptima refers to the ideal nutritional practices for infants, emphasizing the importance of breast milk."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N AL ALTA:Alimentaci\u00f3n al alta refers to the nutritional options available for premature infants upon discharge from the hospital."}{"title": "REALIMENTACI\u00d3N TRAS CIRUG\u00cdA:Realimentaci\u00f3n tras cirug\u00eda refers to the process of reintroducing nutrition after surgical procedures, with specific guidelines based on the type of surgery performed."}{"title": "HIPOXIA FETAL CR\u00d3NICA:Hipoxia fetal cr\u00f3nica is a condition associated with RCIU, indicating chronic low oxygen levels affecting fetal growth."}{"title": "PER\u00cdMETRO CEF\u00c1LICO:Per\u00edmetro cef\u00e1lico is a measurement used to assess head size in newborns, important for evaluating growth and development."}{"title": "MARCADORES BIOQU\u00cdMICOS:MARCADORES BIOQU\u00cdMICOS, or biochemical markers, are utilized to evaluate nutritional status and metabolism in patients. While they serve an important role in assessing these aspects, their reliability can be compromised, particularly in critically ill patients. This highlights the need for careful interpretation of biochemical markers in such contexts."}{"title": "DEPOSICI\u00d3N:Deposici\u00f3n refers to the act of defecation, which is an important factor in assessing gastrointestinal function post-surgery."}{"title": "TR\u00c1NSITO:Tr\u00e1nsito refers to the movement of food through the digestive system, which is monitored post-surgery to determine when to resume feeding."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL MANAGEMENT:Nutritional management encompasses a range of dietary strategies and interventions designed to address the unique needs of patients with various medical conditions. In the context of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), nutritional management focuses on dietary strategies tailored to the specific challenges faced by individuals suffering from this neurodegenerative disease. Additionally, it involves continuous assessment of growth and development to ensure optimal outcomes for patients requiring nutritional support, such as those with renal needs (RNPT).\n\nFurthermore, nutritional management plays a critical role in preventing malnutrition associated with rumination syndrome and is essential for improving health outcomes in patients with pancreatitis. It also includes dietary strategies aimed at treating conditions like chylothorax and chylous effusions, as well as supporting patients with chyle leaks and related disorders. Overall, nutritional management is vital for enhancing the quality of life and health outcomes for patients across a spectrum of medical conditions."}{"title": "GROWTH ASSESSMENT:Growth assessment is the process of evaluating the growth of RNPT after hospital discharge using corrected age."}{"title": "BIOCHEMICAL MARKERS:Periodic determinations of biochemical markers are tools used in the nutritional management of RNPT."}{"title": "GROWTH VELOCITY:Growth velocity is used to monitor the growth of RNPT and assess dietary needs."}{"title": "PATTERNS OF GROWTH:Patterns of growth classification for RNPT at discharge help identify their growth status and needs."}{"title": "EBPN:EBPN refers to a group of extremely low birth weight newborns who have specific nutritional needs and face significant challenges in growth and development. This group is similar to RNMBPN, indicating that both entities share common characteristics related to the nutritional and developmental requirements of newborns with low birth weight."}{"title": "HOSPITAL DISCHARGE:Hospital discharge is the process of releasing RNPT from medical care, requiring careful assessment of their growth patterns."}{"title": "EARLY POSTNATAL CATCH-UP:Early postnatal catch-up refers to the rapid growth that some RNPT experience after birth, which is crucial for their development."}{"title": "GROWTH COMPENSATION:Growth compensation is the process by which RNPT may catch up in growth after experiencing delays."}{"title": "RNMBPN:RNMBPN refers to a group of newborns with specific nutritional needs, particularly those receiving mixed parenteral nutrition, which is a method of providing nutrition intravenously. Although it is not a widely recognized organization, RNMBPN highlights the importance of addressing the unique dietary requirements of these newborns to ensure their health and development."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N INFANTIL:NUTRICI\u00d3N INFANTIL encompasses the field of pediatric nutrition, which is dedicated to ensuring that children receive balanced diets that supply the essential nutrients required for their growth and development. This area of study also includes specific recommendations regarding infant nutrition, with a particular emphasis on the needs of preterm infants. The focus is on promoting healthy dietary practices that support the overall well-being of children from infancy through their developmental stages."}{"title": "LCPUFA:LCPUFA stands for Long-Chain Polyunsaturated Fatty Acids, which are essential nutrients for infant growth and development."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA DE INICIO:Standard infant formula that is recommended for feeding newborns, especially those not breastfed."}{"title": "ALONSO FRANCH M:Alonso Franch M is an author of the study on infant nutrition and bone health published in An Pediatr."}{"title": "BOMBELL S:Bombell S is an author of the Cochrane review on early trophic feeding for very low birth weight infants."}{"title": "CARRASCOSA LEZCANO A:Carrascosa Lezcano A is an author of the Spanish growth study published in An Pediatr."}{"title": "DE MAURO SB:De Mauro SB is an author of the study on feeding intervals and outcomes in very low birth weight infants."}{"title": "FENTON TR:Fenton TR is an author of the new growth chart for preterm babies published in BMC Pediatrics."}{"title": "GRIFFIN I:Griffin I is an author of the study on nutrition of preterm infants after hospital discharge."}{"title": "HAY W:Hay W is an author discussing strategies for feeding preterm infants in Neonatology."}{"title": "KOLETZKO B:Koletzko B is an author of the global standard for the composition of infant formula recommendations."}{"title": "AGGETT P:"}{"title": "ABNORMAL DOPPLER ENTERAL PRESCRIPTION TRIAL COLLABORATIVE GROUP:A collaborative group conducting trials on enteral feeding for preterm growth restricted infants"}{"title": "V. ROQU\u00c9S SERRADILLA:V. Roqu\u00e9s Serradilla is an author contributing to the chapter on neonatal parenteral nutrition"}{"title": "C. FERN\u00c1NDEZ GILINO:C. Fern\u00e1ndez Gilino is an author contributing to the chapter on neonatal parenteral nutrition"}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL NEONATAL:A medical practice involving the intravenous administration of nutrients to patients who cannot meet their nutritional needs through digestion, particularly in newborns"}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N ENTERAL TOTAL:\"ALIMENTACI\u00d3N ENTERAL TOTAL\" refers to the practice of providing complete nutritional support through enteral feeding, particularly for infants. This approach is designed to ensure that infants receive all necessary nutrients directly through the gastrointestinal tract, thereby supporting their growth and development effectively."}{"title": "CATABOLISMO:CATABOLISMO, or catabolism, is a crucial metabolic process that involves the breakdown of molecules to obtain energy. This process can be influenced by various factors, including medications and health conditions. In particular, catabolism tends to increase during illness, which can pose significant challenges for patients. For instance, in burn patients, catabolism is difficult to halt, leading to muscle loss and nutritional difficulties. Additionally, in cases of acute pancreatitis, catabolism accelerates, resulting in a deterioration of nutritional status. This metabolic process is also a concern for premature infants, as their energy needs and nutritional requirements are critical for their development. Overall, catabolism plays a vital role in energy production but can lead to serious health implications under certain conditions."}{"title": "ANABOLISMO:The metabolic process that builds up molecules, crucial for growth and development in premature infants"}{"title": "PREMATUROS:"}{"title": "RECI\u00c9N NACIDO:The term \"reci\u00e9n nacido\" refers to newborns, particularly in the context of their medical care and nutritional needs during the early days of life. Newborns are individuals whose gastrointestinal tracts are exposed to a variety of microorganisms at the time of birth, which plays a significant role in the development of their microbiota. This exposure is crucial for establishing a healthy gut flora, which can impact their overall health and development in the subsequent days and weeks."}{"title": "FLUIDOS Y ELECTROLITOS:Fluids and electrolytes are crucial components for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance in patients, particularly those receiving nutritional support. The management of these elements is especially important in vulnerable populations, such as newborns, where careful monitoring is necessary to prevent complications. Ensuring an appropriate balance of fluids and electrolytes is essential for overall health and recovery in these patients."}{"title": "CUIDADOS NEONATALES:Refers to the specialized medical care provided to newborns, especially those who are premature or have health issues."}{"title": "APORTE PROTEICO-CAL\u00d3RICO:Refers to the ideal nutritional intake of proteins and calories necessary for weight gain in newborns."}{"title": "V\u00cdA DE ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N:Refers to the method of delivering nutrition, either through peripheral or central routes, particularly in newborns."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER VENOSO UMBILICAL:A central venous catheter used in newborns for administering nutrition and medications."}{"title": "BALANCE HIDROELECTROL\u00cdTICO:BALANCE HIDROELECTROL\u00cdTICO refers to the critical process of monitoring and managing the hydroelectrolytic balance in patients, particularly those receiving parenteral nutrition. This balance is essential for maintaining fluid and electrolyte levels, which are vital for overall health. The importance of this management is especially pronounced in vulnerable populations, such as newborns, where precise control of these levels is crucial for their well-being."}{"title": "P\u00c9RDIDAS INSENSIBLES DE AGUA:Refers to the unavoidable loss of water from the body, particularly significant in newborns due to their skin immaturity."}{"title": "TEMPERATURA AMBIENTAL:The environmental temperature that can affect the health and hydration needs of newborns."}{"title": "DIURESIS:Diuresis is defined as the increased production of urine, a physiological process that plays a significant role in managing fluid and electrolyte balance in various patient populations. In the context of patients undergoing dialysis, diuresis can impact their overall fluid and electrolyte status, necessitating careful monitoring and management. Additionally, diuresis is a critical phase in the management of neonates, where the process of urine production is essential for maintaining proper fluid balance. Thus, diuresis is an important factor in both adult and neonatal care, highlighting its relevance in different medical scenarios."}{"title": "NEONATOS:NEONATOS refers to newborn infants, particularly those who are premature and necessitate specialized medical care, especially in the areas of fluid and electrolyte management. Additionally, neonates may present with hyperammonemia, which can arise from urea cycle disorders, thereby requiring careful monitoring and treatment to ensure their health and well-being."}{"title": "HUMEDAD RELATIVA:Relative humidity levels between 80-85% are crucial for the care of neonates in incubators."}{"title": "OLIGURIA:Oliguria is a condition characterized by low urine output, which is a concern in the management of neonates."}{"title": "FASE DIUR\u00c9TICA:The diuretic phase is a critical stage in the management of neonates, where fluid and electrolyte balance is closely monitored."}{"title": "FASE PRE-DIUR\u00c9TICA:The pre-diuretic phase refers to the period before diuresis begins, where careful monitoring of fluid intake and output is essential."}{"title": "NATREMIA:NATREMIA refers to the concentration of sodium in the blood, which is a critical factor in diagnosing and managing conditions such as hyponatremia. It plays an essential role in various physiological functions and is influenced by a range of medical conditions and treatments. Monitoring natremia is particularly important in assessing fluid balance, especially in neonates and in patients undergoing treatment for conditions like Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Overall, natremia serves as a vital indicator of health and is crucial for effective medical management."}{"title": "INCUBADORAS DE DOBLE PARED:"}{"title": "RNT:RNT refers to \"reci\u00e9n nacido a t\u00e9rmino,\" which translates to term newborns. These infants have distinct glucose and nutritional requirements compared to preterm infants. RNT specifically encompasses term newborns who may be receiving parenteral nutrition, adhering to specific nutritional guidelines to meet their needs. Additionally, RNT highlights the importance of nutritional attention for this group of pediatric patients, emphasizing that they require tailored care to support their growth and development."}{"title": "TABELA 2:Table 2 provides recommendations for fluid and electrolyte intake for infants in their first month of life."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS METABOLICA:Metabolic acidosis is a condition that can occur in premature newborns receiving parenteral nutrition due to bicarbonate reabsorption issues."}{"title": "BUN:BUN, or Blood Urea Nitrogen, is a clinical marker that serves as an important indicator of metabolic issues, particularly in infants. It is especially relevant in the context of amino acid administration and parenteral nutrition. Monitoring BUN levels can help healthcare providers assess the metabolic status of infants receiving these treatments, ensuring that any potential complications are identified and addressed promptly."}{"title": "AMINOVEN INFANT:Aminoven Infant is a preparation of amino acids available for nutritional support in infants, specifically designed to supplement cysteine and provide essential nutrients."}{"title": "HIPOTERMIA:Hypothermia is a condition that can affect preterm infants, leading to increased energy requirements for maintaining body temperature."}{"title": "LIPOPLUS:LIPOPLUS is a specialized fat emulsion designed for intravenous nutrition, primarily utilized in parenteral nutrition. It contains a blend of soybean oil, medium-chain triglycerides, and fish oil, which together provide essential fatty acids necessary for patient care. Additionally, LIPOPLUS is recognized as a fourth-generation lipid emulsion that incorporates omega-3 fatty acids, offering potential anti-inflammatory and hepatoprotective effects. The formulation is particularly beneficial in pediatric nutrition, where it combines fish oil with other lipid components to meet the nutritional needs of young patients. Overall, LIPOPLUS serves as a comprehensive solution for delivering vital lipids in various clinical settings."}{"title": "COLESTASIS:Coleostasis is a medical condition characterized by impaired bile flow from the liver to the duodenum. This condition can occur in newborns and is often associated with parenteral nutrition, which is a method of feeding that bypasses the gastrointestinal tract. The inability of bile to flow properly can significantly impact the nutritional status of affected individuals, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing this condition in clinical settings."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES PULMONARES:\"ENFERMEDADES PULMONARES\" refers to respiratory diseases that can significantly affect the health and nutritional needs of newborns. Additionally, these pulmonary diseases may play a role in the development of Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), highlighting their potential impact on various health conditions."}{"title": "HIPOCALEMIA:HIPOCALEMIA refers to two distinct medical conditions: hypokalemia and hypocalcemia. \n\nHypokalemia is characterized by low potassium levels in the blood, which can lead to various complications, including nephrogenic diabetes insipidus. It can be caused by renal disorders or excessive loss of potassium, and may result in symptoms such as muscle weakness and arrhythmias. Additionally, hypokalemia can affect urinary composition and contribute to stone formation.\n\nOn the other hand, hypocalcemia is a condition marked by low calcium levels in the blood. This condition can occur in premature newborns due to inadequate calcium reserves, as well as in patients with eating disorders due to nutritional deficiencies. Hypocalcemia can also arise from parathyroid dysfunction, magnesium metabolism issues, elevated phosphorus levels, and is a concern in patients with chronic kidney disease. It may manifest as a complication in patients with diabetic ketoacidosis. Treatment for hypocalcemia often involves vitamin D and its metabolites to help restore calcium levels.\n\nIn summary, HIPOCALEMIA encompasses both hypokalemia and hypocalcemia, each with distinct causes, symptoms, and treatment approaches related to their respective electrolyte imbalances."}{"title": "HIPOFOSFOREMIA:Hipofosfatemia, also known as hypophosphatemia, is a medical condition characterized by low phosphorus levels in the blood. This condition can arise from various factors, including inadequate intake of phosphorus, particularly in newborns. Additionally, hypophosphatemia is often observed in patients who are on parenteral nutrition, necessitating careful management to address the deficiency."}{"title": "KERNICTERUS:Kernicterus is a type of brain damage that can occur in newborns with severe jaundice, which can be a risk in cases of hyperbilirubinemia."}{"title": "DBP:DBP refers to two distinct concepts: a type of bariatric surgery and developmental brain injury. In the context of bariatric surgery, DBP is a malabsorptive technique that may require patients to make dietary adjustments and take nutritional supplements to address potential deficiencies, such as vitamin A deficiency. This highlights the importance of nutritional assessment for individuals undergoing this procedure. On the other hand, DBP also denotes developmental brain injury, which is a significant concern for premature newborns, as it is closely related to their nutritional needs. Thus, DBP encompasses both a surgical approach with implications for dietary management and a medical condition that underscores the critical role of nutrition in early development."}{"title": "PEDITRACE:PEDITRACE is a pediatric multi-trace element solution used for the nutritional needs of preterm infants."}{"title": "OLIGO-ZINC:Oligo-zinc is a zinc supplement designed for use in preterm infants to meet their nutritional requirements."}{"title": "INFUVITE PEDI\u00c1TRICO:INFUVITE PEDI\u00c1TRICO is a specialized vitamin preparation designed for infants, particularly aimed at meeting the nutritional needs of preterm infants. The product consists of two vials that provide essential nutritional supplementation, ensuring that infants receive the necessary vitamins for their growth and development."}{"title": "CARNITINA:Carnitina, also known as carnitine, is a vital substance that plays a crucial role in the transport of long-chain fatty acids into the mitochondria for oxidation, which is essential for energy production in the body. This process is particularly relevant for long-chain fatty acids and is important for various populations, including preterm infants. The levels of carnitina are monitored in patients undergoing dietary treatment to ensure adequate energy production. While carnitina is often recommended as a supplement, it is advised to be used only when levels are low or when symptoms of deficiency appear, as its empirical use lacks clear evidence. Overall, carnitina is an amino acid that is integral to metabolic processes and energy generation in the body."}{"title": "COPPER:Copper, also known as \"cobre,\" is an essential trace mineral that plays a vital role in various bodily functions. It is necessary for health in low concentrations but can be toxic at high levels. The dietary reference intake for copper varies across different age groups, and specific intake recommendations are outlined in dietary guidelines. \n\nDeficiency of copper is common in certain medical conditions, such as after biliopancreatic diversion and in patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation, which can lead to various health issues. In infants receiving nutritional supplementation, copper levels are closely monitored to prevent toxicity. Excessive copper can lead to serious health conditions, including Wilson's disease, and may contribute to oxidative stress, potentially impacting neurodegenerative diseases.\n\nCopper is also studied for its potential role in various diseases, including cancer. In the context of parenteral nutrition, copper is considered a contaminant, and its levels should be carefully managed to avoid toxicity. Overall, copper is a crucial micronutrient that must be maintained within a balanced range to support health effectively."}{"title": "SELENIUM:Selenium is a trace mineral that plays a critical role in various bodily functions and is essential for overall health. It is recognized for its antioxidant properties and is involved in metabolism. The dietary reference intake for selenium varies by age group, with recommended daily intake levels typically ranging from 50 to 70 \u03bcg/day in certain cases. While selenium is not routinely required, it may be recommended for individuals with specific health conditions, including those undergoing dietary treatment or suffering from chronic diseases.\n\nSelenium is particularly important for infant nutrition and is included in multi-trace element solutions. Its deficiency has been reported in patients with cirrhosis and other chronic health issues, which can adversely affect their overall health. Additionally, selenium is being studied for its potential health benefits, including its role in cancer prevention and cardiovascular health, as well as its significance in managing liver disease. Overall, selenium is a vital micronutrient that contributes to various aspects of health and well-being."}{"title": "MANGANESE:Manganese is a trace element that plays a significant role in nutritional supplementation, particularly for infants. It is important to monitor manganese levels in such contexts to ensure adequate intake. However, manganese should be minimized in parenteral nutrition due to the potential risk of toxicity. The dietary reference intake for manganese is specified for different age groups in nutritional guidelines, highlighting its importance as a mineral. These guidelines outline recommended daily intake levels for manganese, ensuring that individuals receive appropriate amounts based on their age and nutritional needs."}{"title": "NEONATES:Neonates are newborn infants who are particularly characterized by their need for specialized nutritional support, including parenteral nutrition and specific lipid solutions. These infants may exhibit unique intestinal adaptation capabilities that differentiate them from older children and adults, highlighting their distinct nutritional and developmental needs."}{"title": "RECI\u00c9N NACIDOS A T\u00c9RMINO:Reci\u00e9n nacidos a t\u00e9rmino are newborns born at or after 37 weeks of gestation, who may also require nutritional support."}{"title": "ACIDO ASC\u00d3RBICO:Ascorbic acid, commonly known as Vitamin C, is included in Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico for its antioxidant properties and role in collagen synthesis."}{"title": "ACIDO PANTOT\u00c9NICO:Pantothenic acid, or Vitamin B5, is a water-soluble vitamin important for the synthesis of coenzyme A, included in Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico."}{"title": "ACIDO F\u00d3LICO:ACIDO F\u00d3LICO, also known as Vitamin B9, is a vital micronutrient essential for various physiological functions, particularly in older adults, where it helps prevent deficiencies and related health issues. It plays a crucial role in DNA synthesis and repair, making it an important component in parenteral nutrition formulations to support cell division. Additionally, Folic acid is included in products like Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico, highlighting its significance in both adult and pediatric health."}{"title": "VIAL 2:Vial 2 is part of the Infuvite Pedi\u00e1trico solution, containing 1ml of the vitamin mixture."}{"title": "NRPT:NRPT refers to the nutritional requirements for preterm infants, which are outlined in the guidelines for vitamin supplementation."}{"title": "VIAL 1:"}{"title": "FARMACIA:Farmacia is the pharmacy department dedicated to providing medications and nutritional support to patients. It plays a crucial role in preparing parenteral nutrition under sterile conditions, ensuring both safety and efficacy in the delivery of these essential health services."}{"title": "GASOMETR\u00cdA:Gasometry is a medical test performed to assess the levels of gases in the blood, important for monitoring patients on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "NIACINAMIDA:Niacinamide is a form of Vitamin B3 included in parenteral nutrition to support skin health and metabolism."}{"title": "DEXPANTHENAL:Dexpanthenol is a form of Vitamin B5 included in parenteral nutrition that aids in the healing process and skin health."}{"title": "VITAMINA K1:Vitamin K1, also known as Phylloquinone, is a vital nutrient found in plants that plays a crucial role in supporting blood clotting and maintaining bone health. It is often included in parenteral nutrition to ensure adequate levels of this essential vitamin, which is necessary for the proper functioning of the coagulation process in the body."}{"title": "D3:"}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR PAEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY, HEPATOLOGY, AND NUTRITION:A professional organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for pediatric nutrition, particularly for preterm infants."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF PAEDIATRIC RESEARCH:A society that promotes research in pediatric health and nutrition, supporting studies and guidelines for better health outcomes in children."}{"title": "J PEDIATR GASTROENTEROL NUTR:The \"J PEDIATR GASTROENTEROL NUTR,\" also known as the Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition, is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research and guidelines pertinent to the fields of pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition. The journal features a variety of studies, including those focused on pediatric gastrointestinal health and specific conditions such as cystic fibrosis. It serves as a vital resource for professionals in the field, contributing to the advancement of knowledge and practices related to the nutritional and gastrointestinal well-being of children."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL NEEDS OF THE PRETERM INFANT:A guideline published by the American Academy of Pediatrics addressing the specific nutritional requirements for preterm infants."}{"title": "HILLTOP TRIAL:A randomized controlled trial investigating the use of heparin in total parenteral nutrition to prevent sepsis in neonates."}{"title": "NUTRITION OF THE PRETERM INFANT:A comprehensive overview of the nutritional requirements and guidelines for preterm infants."}{"title": "BUONOCORE G:Buonocore G is a co-author of a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "CARNIELLI VP:Carnelli VP is a co-author of a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "DE CURTIS M:De Curtis M is a prominent researcher in the field of neonatal nutrition, particularly focusing on the nutritional needs of preterm infants. They have co-authored a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants, which was published in the Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition. Additionally, De Curtis M contributed to a document addressing the nutrition of preterm infants, published in Early Human Development. Their research also encompasses the study of parenteral nutrition in premature infants, highlighting their commitment to improving nutritional strategies for this vulnerable population."}{"title": "DARMUAN D:Darmaun D is a co-author of a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "DECSI T:Decsi T is a co-author of a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "ALONSO P\u00c9REZ L:Alonso P\u00e9rez L is a co-author of a study on intravenous lipid emulsions in pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Acta Pediatr Esp."}{"title": "FERN\u00c1NDEZ V\u00c1ZQUEZ A:Fern\u00e1ndez V\u00e1zquez A is a co-author of a study on intravenous lipid emulsions in pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Acta Pediatr Esp."}{"title": "GOMIS MU\u00d1OZ P:Gomis Mu\u00f1oz P is a notable figure in the field of pediatric nutrition and healthcare. He is a co-author of a consensus document on pediatric parenteral nutrition, which was published in the journal Nutr Hosp. Additionally, he has contributed to a study focused on intravenous lipid emulsions in pediatric parenteral nutrition, published in Acta Pediatr Esp. Furthermore, Gomis Mu\u00f1oz P has also engaged in research concerning sealing methods in pediatric patients, showcasing his diverse contributions to improving pediatric care and nutrition."}{"title": "MORENO VILLARES JM:Moreno Villares JM is a notable figure in the field of pediatric nutrition, particularly in the area of parenteral nutrition. He is a co-author of a consensus document on pediatric parenteral nutrition, which was published in the journal Nutr Hosp. Additionally, he contributed as a co-author to a study focusing on intravenous lipid emulsions in pediatric parenteral nutrition, published in Acta Pediatr Esp. Furthermore, Moreno Villares JM has been involved in research concerning sealing methods for pediatric patients who require home parenteral nutrition. His work reflects a commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in pediatric nutritional care."}{"title": "BASSIOUNY M:Bassiouny M is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial on parenteral nutrition and chronic lung diseases in preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "ALMARSFAWY H:Almarsafawy H is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial on parenteral nutrition and chronic lung diseases in preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "ABDEL-HADY H:Abdel-Hady H is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial on parenteral nutrition and chronic lung diseases in preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "NASEF N:Nasef N is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial on parenteral nutrition and chronic lung diseases in preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "HAMMAD TA:Hammad TA is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial on parenteral nutrition and chronic lung diseases in preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "ALY H:Aly H is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial on parenteral nutrition and chronic lung diseases in preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr."}{"title": "BIRCH P:Birch P is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial of heparin in total parenteral nutrition published in Arch Dis Child Fetal Neonatal Ed."}{"title": "OGDEN S:Ogden S is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial of heparin in total parenteral nutrition published in Arch Dis Child Fetal Neonatal Ed."}{"title": "HEWSON M:Hewson M is a co-author of a randomized controlled trial of heparin in total parenteral nutrition published in Arch Dis Child Fetal Neonatal Ed."}{"title": "RIGO J:Rigo J is a prominent researcher in the field of pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition. He has co-authored a significant document on the nutrition of preterm infants, which was published in the journal Early Human Development. Additionally, Rigo J has contributed to discussions surrounding parenteral nutrition specifically for premature infants, highlighting his expertise and involvement in this critical area of pediatric health."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ L\u00d3PEZ L:G\u00f3mez L\u00f3pez L is a co-author of a consensus document on pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Nutr Hosp."}{"title": "P\u00c9REZ-PORTABELLA MARISTANY C:P\u00e9rez-Portabella Maristany C is a co-author of a consensus document on pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Nutr Hosp."}{"title": "GRAND A:Grand A is a co-author of a study on the influence of vitamins and trace elements on lipid peroxidation in neonatal parenteral nutrition published in JPEN J Parenter Enter Nutr."}{"title": "JALABERT A:Jalabert A is a co-author of a study on the influence of vitamins and trace elements on lipid peroxidation in neonatal parenteral nutrition published in JPEN J Parenter Enter Nutr."}{"title": "MERCIER G:Mercier G is a co-author of a study on the influence of vitamins and trace elements on lipid peroxidation in neonatal parenteral nutrition published in JPEN J Parenter Enter Nutr."}{"title": "FLORENT M:Florent M is a co-author of a study on the influence of vitamins and trace elements on lipid peroxidation in neonatal parenteral nutrition published in JPEN J Parenter Enter Nutr."}{"title": "HANSEL-ESTELLER S:Hansel-Esteller S is a co-author of a study on the influence of vitamins and trace elements on lipid peroxidation in neonatal parenteral nutrition published in JPEN J Parenter Enter Nutr."}{"title": "CAMBONIE G:Cambonie G is a co-author of a study on the influence of vitamins and trace elements on lipid peroxidation in neonatal parenteral nutrition published in JPEN J Parenter Enter Nutr."}{"title": "HERN\u00c1NDEZ PRAT C:Hern\u00e1ndez Prat C is a co-author of a study on destabilization of lipids in pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Farm Hosp."}{"title": "REAL PANISELLO MA:Real Panisello MA is a co-author of a study on destabilization of lipids in pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Farm Hosp."}{"title": "FUENTES BONMAT\u00cd MJ:Fuentes Bonmat\u00ed MJ is a co-author of a study on destabilization of lipids in pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Farm Hosp."}{"title": "TORRES CHAZARRA C:Torres Chazarra C is a co-author of a study on destabilization of lipids in pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Farm Hosp."}{"title": "S\u00c1NCHEZ CASADO MI:S\u00e1nchez Casado MI is a co-author of a study on destabilization of lipids in pediatric parenteral nutrition published in Farm Hosp."}{"title": "IACOBELLI S:Iacobelli S is a co-author of a study on standardized parenteral nutrition in preterm infants published in Neonatology."}{"title": "BONSANTE F:Bonsante F is a co-author of a study on standardized parenteral nutrition in preterm infants published in"}{"title": "C. FUENTES SOCORRO:C. Fuentes Socorro is one of the authors discussing complications related to long-term central venous catheters in pediatrics."}{"title": "I. VITORIA MI\u00d1ANA:I. Vitoria Mi\u00f1ana is one of the authors discussing complications related to long-term central venous catheters in pediatrics."}{"title": "C. RIBES KONINCKX:C. Ribes Koninckx is one of the authors discussing complications related to long-term central venous catheters in pediatrics."}{"title": "R. SANCH\u00cdS RAMADA:R. Sanch\u00eds Ramada is one of the authors discussing complications related to long-term central venous catheters in pediatrics."}{"title": "C. GUTI\u00c9RREZ SAN ROMAN:C. Guti\u00e9rrez San Roman is one of the authors discussing complications related to long-term central venous catheters in pediatrics."}{"title": "CENTRAL VENOUS CATHETERS:Central venous catheters are medical devices designed to be inserted into a large vein, providing long-term access to the bloodstream for various medical treatments. They are particularly useful for long-term intravenous access, allowing for the administration of medications, fluids, and nutrients. However, it is important to note that the use of central venous catheters can lead to complications, especially in pediatric patients."}{"title": "OBSTRUCTION OF CENTRAL VENOUS CATHETERS:Obstruction of central venous catheters is a complication that can occur in 14-36% of cases, affecting their functionality."}{"title": "GASTROINTESTINAL PRIMING:Gastrointestinal priming is a feeding strategy aimed at preparing the digestive system of preterm infants for enteral feeding."}{"title": "THROMBOSIS:Thrombosis refers to the formation of a blood clot inside a blood vessel, which can complicate the use of central venous catheters in pediatric patients."}{"title": "CATHETER OCLUSION:Catheter occlusion is a blockage that prevents the normal flow of fluids through a catheter, often requiring medical intervention."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL STRATEGIES:Nutritional strategies are planned approaches designed to enhance dietary intake and improve the nutritional status of patients, particularly those with specific medical conditions such as liver disease and acute pancreatitis. These strategies aim to provide adequate nutrition tailored to the unique needs of individuals facing these health challenges."}{"title": "UROKINASA:Urokinase is a medication used as a thrombolytic agent to dissolve blood clots."}{"title": "ALTEPLASA:Alteplase is a medication utilized primarily for fibrinolysis, particularly in patients experiencing ischemic stroke, where it aids in dissolving blood clots. It serves as a fibrinolytic agent and is also indicated for treating catheter occlusions. In the context of acute ischemic stroke, alteplase is employed for thrombolysis, although its administration may sometimes need to be interrupted shortly after initiation. Overall, alteplase is recognized for its effectiveness in managing blood clots across various medical conditions."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS INTRALUMINAL:Trombosis intraluminal refers to the formation of a thrombus within the lumen of a catheter, leading to partial or complete obstruction."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS EXTRALUMINAL:Trombosis extraluminal refers to the formation of a thrombus outside the catheter, which can also lead to obstruction."}{"title": "M\u00c9DICO RESPONSABLE:The \"M\u00c9DICO RESPONSABLE\" is the professional responsible for ensuring that patients receive the necessary information and uphold their right to informed consent. Additionally, this physician oversees the treatment and management of patients dealing with catheter-related issues, ensuring comprehensive care and support throughout the patient's medical journey."}{"title": "CATETEROGRAF\u00cdA:Cateterograf\u00eda is a diagnostic procedure that involves the administration of contrast through a catheter. This technique is utilized to identify and evaluate mechanical or thrombotic issues within the body. By using a catheter to deliver the contrast agent, healthcare professionals can obtain detailed images and insights into the vascular system, aiding in the diagnosis and management of various medical conditions."}{"title": "ECOGRAF\u00cdA:ECOGRAF\u00cdA, also known as ultrasound, is a diagnostic imaging technique utilized for various medical evaluations. It is primarily employed to assess liver and pancreatic lesions in patients. Additionally, ECOGRAF\u00cdA is effective in detecting obstructions and the presence of thrombi in catheters, making it a valuable tool in diagnosing vascular issues. This imaging procedure plays a crucial role in providing insights into both organ health and potential complications related to catheter use."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME PINCH-OFF:S\u00edndrome pinch-off occurs when a portion of the catheter is compressed between the clavicle and the first rib, potentially leading to complications."}{"title": "TROMBO MURAL:Trombo mural refers to a thrombus that forms on the wall of the catheter, which can lead to obstruction."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS VENOSA:Trombosis venosa, or venous thrombosis, is a serious complication that can arise during the maintenance of central venous catheters (CVCs). This condition is characterized by the formation of blood clots in the veins, which can occur in patients who have long-term CVCs. The presence of these clots can lead to significant clinical manifestations, including the potential loss of venous access. In severe cases, this complication may necessitate intestinal transplantation. Overall, thrombosis venosa is a critical concern associated with catheter use, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing patients with central venous catheters to prevent such adverse outcomes."}{"title": "FIBRINA:"}{"title": "D-D\u00cdMEROS:D-d\u00edmeros are a laboratory test used to assess the presence of thrombotic events, with levels above 500 mg/ml indicating a potential issue."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME POSTFLEBITICO:S\u00edndrome postfleb\u00edtico is a condition that may develop as a complication of venous thrombosis, characterized by edema, pain, and skin changes."}{"title": "HICKMAN CVC:"}{"title": "TROMBOLISIS:Trombolysis is a medical procedure designed to dissolve blood clots that obstruct blood vessels. It is indicated for use in patients under specific circumstances to ensure effective treatment. This procedure plays a crucial role in managing conditions where blood flow is compromised due to clot formation."}{"title": "HEPARINIZACI\u00d3N:Heparinization refers to the administration of low molecular weight heparins for the treatment and prophylaxis of thrombotic events."}{"title": "ANTICOAGULACI\u00d3N:Anticoagulation is a treatment method that involves the use of anticoagulant medications to prevent blood clots from forming or growing."}{"title": "TROMBOL\u00cdTICO:Trombolytic therapy involves the use of drugs to dissolve blood clots that are obstructing blood flow to vital organs."}{"title": "HEPARINAS DE BAJO PESO MOLECULAR:Low molecular weight heparins (LMWH) are anticoagulant medications used for the prevention and treatment of thromboembolic disorders."}{"title": "D\u00cdMEROS D:D-dimer is a fibrin degradation product that is typically elevated in the presence of a blood clot, used as a diagnostic marker in thrombotic conditions."}{"title": "FIBRIN\u00d3GENO:Fibrinogen is a crucial blood plasma protein that plays a vital role in blood clot formation and wound healing. It is essential for the coagulation process, helping to prevent excessive bleeding when injuries occur. Additionally, fibrinogen levels are closely monitored in patients undergoing anticoagulation therapy and those with thrombotic conditions, as these levels can indicate the body's ability to form clots effectively. Overall, fibrinogen is integral to maintaining hemostasis and is a key factor in the management of various blood-related health issues."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS:Thrombosis is a medical condition characterized by the formation of a blood clot within a blood vessel. This condition can lead to significant complications, particularly during venous access procedures. It is also noted as a potential complication associated with central parenteral nutrition. The presence of thrombosis can complicate medical interventions and may pose risks to patient health."}{"title": "CL\u00cdNICA DE TROMBOSIS VENOSA:Cl\u00ednica de Trombosis Venosa specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of venous thrombosis."}{"title": "INFECCI\u00d3N RELACIONADA CON CVC:Infecci\u00f3n relacionada con CVC describes infections that occur due to the presence of a central venous catheter, including local and systemic infections."}{"title": "STAPHILOCOCO COAGULASA NEGATIVO:Staphylococcus coagulase-negative is a type of bacteria frequently associated with infections in patients with CVC."}{"title": "S. AUREUS:S. Aureus, also known as Staphylococcus aureus, is a type of bacteria that can lead to various infections. It is commonly associated with skin and respiratory flora and poses a particular risk to individuals with compromised health. This bacterium is known for its ability to cause a range of infections, highlighting its significance in both clinical and community settings."}{"title": "ENTEROCOCO:Enterococcus, also referred to as Enterococo, is a genus of bacteria that is commonly found as part of the normal intestinal flora. However, it has the potential to cause infections, particularly in patients with weakened immune systems or those with central venous catheters (CVC). These infections can be serious and are more likely to occur in individuals who are already vulnerable due to underlying health conditions."}{"title": "PSEUDOMONAS:Pseudomonas is a genus of bacteria that can cause infections, particularly in immunocompromised patients."}{"title": "CANDIDA SPP.:Candida species are fungi that can cause infections, especially in patients with prolonged neutropenia or those undergoing certain treatments."}{"title": "DETECCI\u00d3N DE TROMBOSIS VENOSA:Detection of venous thrombosis involves various diagnostic procedures to confirm the presence of thrombus in the venous system."}{"title": "NO DETECCI\u00d3N DE TROMBOSIS VENOSA:No detection of venous thrombosis indicates that despite clinical suspicion, no thrombus was found."}{"title": "VALORAR ESTUDIO TROMBOFILIA:Evaluating thrombophilia involves assessing selected cases for underlying conditions that predispose individuals to thrombosis."}{"title": "MONITORIZACI\u00d3N:Monitoring refers to the ongoing assessment of patients, particularly those undergoing treatment for thrombosis, to ensure effective management and detect complications."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS S\u00c9PTICA:Septic thrombosis refers to the presence of a thrombus associated with a systemic infection, leading to complications."}{"title": "ENDOCARDITIS:Endocarditis is an infection of the inner lining of the heart, often considered a serious complication that can arise from catheter-related infections. It is particularly associated with patients who have central venous catheters (CVC). This condition poses significant health risks and requires careful management to prevent severe outcomes."}{"title": "MET\u00c1STASIS A DISTANCIA:Distant metastasis refers to the spread of cancer cells from the original tumor site to other parts of the body, which can complicate treatment in patients with CVC."}{"title": "G\u00c9RMENES GRAM POSITIVOS:Gram-positive germs are a category of bacteria that are frequently involved in infections, particularly in patients with CVC."}{"title": "BACILOS GRAM NEGATIVOS:Gram-negative bacilli are a type of bacteria that can cause infections, especially in patients with compromised immune systems."}{"title": "LEVAUDURAS:Yeasts, particularly Candida species, are fungi that can lead to infections in certain patient populations, especially those with weakened immune systems.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CANDIDA:Candida is a genus of yeasts that can cause infections, especially in immunocompromised patients, and is often associated with neutropenia and other serious conditions."}{"title": "BGC:Bacilos Gram negativos (BGN) are a group of bacteria that can cause infections, particularly in the gastrointestinal tract."}{"title": "CL\u00cdNICA:Cl\u00ednica refers to healthcare facilities where professionals apply nutritional assessment methods to enhance patient care. Additionally, it encompasses the clinical presentation of infections associated with catheters, detailing symptoms and diagnostic criteria for sepsis and other related complications. This dual focus highlights the importance of both nutritional support and infection management within clinical settings."}{"title": "HEMOCULTIVOS:Hemocultures are tests used to detect the presence of bacteria or fungi in the blood, crucial for diagnosing bacteremia related to catheters."}{"title": "ANTIBIOTERAPIA:Antibioterapia refers to the treatment of infections through the use of antibiotics. This therapy may be tailored according to culture results to ensure effective management of the infection. Additionally, antibiotic therapy is essential in addressing complications that may arise from intestinal failure, highlighting its critical role in both infection management and the treatment of related health issues."}{"title": "OSTEOMIELITIS:Osteomyelitis is an infection in the bone that can occur as a complication of severe infections related to central venous catheters."}{"title": "NEUTROPENIA:Neutropenia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of neutrophils, a type of white blood cell essential for fighting off infections. This condition leads to an increased susceptibility to infections, particularly in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type Ib (GSDIb). Additionally, the low neutrophil count associated with neutropenia can influence dietary choices due to the heightened risk of infections. Neutropenia can occur in individuals with GSDIb, further complicating their health management."}{"title": "C. GALBRATA:C. Galbrata is a contributor to the bibliographic references related to pediatric radiology and thrombolytic therapy in children."}{"title": "LA FE DEPARTAMENT DE SALUT:La Fe Departament de Salut is a healthcare organization involved in nutritional diagnosis and follow-up protocols."}{"title": "VALENCIANA:Valenciana refers to the region associated with the La Fe healthcare facility."}{"title": "PROTOCOLO DE DIAGN\u00d3STICO Y SEGUIMIENTO NUTRICIONAL DE LA DISFAGIA:The \"PROTOCOLO DE DIAGN\u00d3STICO Y SEGUIMIENTO NUTRICIONAL DE LA DISFAGIA\" is a comprehensive protocol designed for the diagnosis and monitoring of dysphagia. It details specific procedures and assessments aimed at ensuring safe swallowing for patients experiencing this condition. The protocol not only focuses on the diagnostic aspects but also emphasizes the importance of nutritional follow-up for individuals with dysphagia. It provides guidelines for safe eating practices, ensuring that patients receive appropriate recommendations to manage their condition effectively. Overall, this protocol serves as a crucial resource for healthcare professionals in the assessment and ongoing care of dysphagia patients."}{"title": "OWEN A:Owen A is an author of a study on malfunctioning central venous catheters in children."}{"title": "ROEBUCK D:Roebuck D is an author of a study on malfunctioning central venous catheters in children."}{"title": "HIORNS M:Hiorns M is an author of a study on malfunctioning central venous catheters in children."}{"title": "BASKIN J:Baskin J is an author of a study on the management of occlusion and thrombosis associated with long-term indwelling central venous catheters."}{"title": "PUI C:Pui C is an author of a study on the management of occlusion and thrombosis associated with long-term indwelling central venous catheters."}{"title": "REISS U:Reiss U is an author of a study on the management of occlusion and thrombosis associated with long-term indwelling central venous catheters."}{"title": "WILIMAS JA:Wilimas JA is an author of a study on the management of occlusion and thrombosis associated with long-term indwelling central venous catheters."}{"title": "METZGER ML:Metzger ML is an author of a study on the management of occlusion and thrombosis associated with long-term indwelling central venous catheters."}{"title": "RIBEIRO RC:Ribeiro RC is an author of a study on the management of occlusion and thrombosis associated with long-term indwelling central venous catheters."}{"title": "GOLDENBERG NA:Goldenberg NA is an author of a study on thrombolytic regimens for high-risk deep venous thrombosis in children."}{"title": "DURHAM JD:Durham JD is an author of a study on thrombolytic regimens for high-risk deep venous thrombosis in children."}{"title": "KNAPP-CLEVENGER R:Knapp-Clevenger R is an author of a study on thrombolytic regimens for high-risk deep venous thrombosis in children."}{"title": "MANCO-JOHNSON MJ:Manco-Johnson MJ is an author of a study on thrombolytic regimens for high-risk deep venous thrombosis in children."}{"title": "CROWTHER M:Crowther M is an author known for conducting systematic reviews in the medical field. Notably, Crowther M authored a systematic review on post-thrombotic syndrome in children, contributing valuable insights into this condition. Additionally, Crowther M also conducted a systematic review focused on glutamine supplementation in stem cell transplantation, further showcasing expertise in the area of clinical research and its implications for patient care."}{"title": "KENET G:Kenet G is an author of a systematic review on post-thrombotic syndrome in children."}{"title": "NOWAK-G\u00d6TTL U:Nowak-G\u00f6ttl U is an author of a systematic review on post-thrombotic syndrome in children."}{"title": "MALE C:Male C is an author of a study on the association between central venous line placement and venous thrombosis risk in children."}{"title": "JULIAN JA:Julian JA is an author of a study on the association between central venous line placement and venous thrombosis risk in children."}{"title": "MASSICOTTE P:Massicotte P is an author of a study on the association between central venous line placement and venous thrombosis risk in children."}{"title": "GENT M:Gent M is an author of a study on the association between central venous line placement and venous thrombosis risk in children."}{"title": "MITCHELL L:Mitchell L is an author of a study on the association between central venous line placement and venous thrombosis risk in children."}{"title": "BARNACLE A:"}{"title": "ACV:ACV, or Accidente Vascular Cerebral, is a medical event commonly known as a stroke. It is particularly significant in the elderly population, as it can lead to various complications, including swallowing difficulties. Additionally, ACV is associated with central nervous system disorders and can be a contributing factor to conditions such as Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH)."}{"title": "SALA DE NEUROLOG\u00cdA:The Neurology ward is a medical facility where patients with neurological disorders, including dysphagia, are treated."}{"title": "SALA DE NEUROCIRUG\u00cdA:The Neurosurgery ward is a medical facility specializing in surgical interventions for neurological conditions, which may include patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA TOR\u00c1CICA:The Thoracic Surgery department focuses on surgical treatments for conditions affecting the thoracic cavity, which can impact swallowing."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA CARD\u00cdACA:The Cardiac Surgery department specializes in surgical procedures for heart conditions, which may also relate to dysphagia."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA TIROIDEA:The Thyroid Surgery department deals with surgical interventions on the thyroid gland, which can affect swallowing."}{"title": "ORL:ORL refers to the Otolaryngology department, also known as Otorrinolaringolog\u00eda, which specializes in the evaluation and treatment of conditions affecting the ear, nose, and throat. This department is involved in the patient's treatment and follow-up care, particularly in cases such as laryngeal carcinoma. Additionally, ORL encompasses hospital wards where dysphagia screening is protocolized for patients, highlighting its role in managing conditions that may lead to swallowing difficulties. Overall, ORL plays a crucial role in the comprehensive care of patients with various otolaryngological issues, including those that may cause dysphagia."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA MAXILO-FACIAL:The Maxillofacial Surgery department focuses on surgical treatment of conditions affecting the face and jaw, which can impact swallowing."}{"title": "UMCE:UMCE refers to a specific medical unit that focuses on patients at risk of dysphagia. Within this unit, hospital wards have implemented a protocol for dysphagia screening to ensure that patients receive appropriate care and assessment related to their swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "UMLE:UMLE is an organization involved in the protocolized treatment of patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. It operates within hospital wards where dysphagia screening is systematically implemented for patients. Additionally, UMLE may refer to another medical unit that specializes in the assessment and treatment of dysphagia, further emphasizing its role in ensuring comprehensive care for individuals with this condition."}{"title": "ANXIETAD:Anxiety is a psychological condition that may arise in patients dealing with the challenges of dysphagia."}{"title": "EATING-ASSESSMENT TOOL-10:The Eating-Assessment Tool-10 (EAT-10) is a tool designed to detect individuals who may suffer from dysphagia and identify those who need further evaluation."}{"title": "REV002:REV002 is a protocol for the diagnosis and nutritional follow-up of dysphagia, established in June 2013."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL PROTOCOL FOR DYSPHAGIA:A protocol for diagnosing and monitoring nutritional needs in patients with dysphagia, including dietary recommendations and assessments."}{"title": "NUTILIS:Nutilis is a thickening agent utilized in both hospital settings and nutritional products. It is specifically designed to assist patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing, by modifying the consistency of liquids to ensure they are safe and easier to consume. Nutilis plays a crucial role in helping these patients achieve the appropriate food consistency, thereby enhancing their ability to eat and drink safely."}{"title": "NEUROLOGY AND NEUROSURGERY WARDS:Hospital wards where dysphagia screening is protocolized for patients."}{"title": "THORACIC AND CARDIAC SURGERY:Hospital wards where dysphagia screening is protocolized for patients."}{"title": "THYROID SURGERY:Hospital wards where dysphagia screening is protocolized for patients."}{"title": "MAXILLO-FACIAL SURGERY:Hospital wards where dysphagia screening is protocolized for patients."}{"title": "INTERNAL MEDICINE:Hospital wards where dysphagia screening is protocolized for patients."}{"title": "CRUSHED DIET:A dietary plan consisting of two plates and dessert, suitable for patients with dysphagia, providing medium caloric value."}{"title": "EASY SWALLOWING DIET \u2013 DYSPHAGIA:A dietary plan consisting of two plates, milk bread, and dessert, designed for patients transitioning to a regular diet, providing high caloric value."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL VALUE:The energy, protein, carbohydrate, and fat content of the diets provided for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "THICKENING AGENTS:Substances used to modify the consistency of food and liquids for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "DIET OF STARTING CRUSHED:"}{"title": "ESPESANTE:ESPESANTE is a thickening agent designed to modify the texture of liquids and foods for individuals with swallowing difficulties. It ensures safe consumption by altering the consistency of these substances, making them easier to swallow. The product is particularly beneficial for patients who require dietary modifications to prevent choking or aspiration. Nutilis is another name associated with this thickening agent, emphasizing its role in enhancing the safety and comfort of those with dysphagia."}{"title": "NUTRICIONAL:The term \"NUTRICIONAL\" encompasses a range of nutritional attributes and requirements essential for various patient populations. It highlights the importance of nutritional assessment as a dynamic process, particularly for burn patients, to ensure they receive adequate support for recovery. Additionally, it is crucial for patients undergoing bariatric surgery, as proper nutritional evaluation helps facilitate weight loss and prevent potential complications. Nutritional education plays a significant role in this context, aiming to alter patients' beliefs and behaviors regarding food to encourage healthier eating habits. Furthermore, \"NUTRICIONAL\" also pertains to dietary interventions and management strategies for patients, especially those in oncology, as well as the nutritional assessment and management aspects of the dysphagia protocol. Overall, the concept of \"NUTRICIONAL\" is integral to promoting optimal health outcomes across various medical conditions."}{"title": "ALTA:ALTA refers to the discharge or release of a patient from medical care, marking the conclusion of treatment or monitoring for various medical conditions. This term is often discussed in the context of recovery from conditions such as diabetic ketoacidosis (cetoacidosis diab\u00e9tica) and is also relevant in the discharge process for patients with dysphagia. In both cases, ALTA signifies that the patient has reached a stage where they no longer require ongoing medical intervention."}{"title": "FAMILIAR:A family member is someone who may assist or supervise a patient with dysphagia during meals to prevent choking."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE MEDICINA F\u00cdSICA Y REHABILITACI\u00d3N:The Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Service includes a unit for speech therapy, focusing on rehabilitation for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE OTORRINOLARINGOLOG\u00cdA:The Otolaryngology Service specializes in disorders related to the ear, nose, and throat, including issues that may affect swallowing."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE MEDICINA INTERNA:The Internal Medicine Service provides comprehensive care for patients, including those with dysphagia in the Medium and Long Stay Unit."}{"title": "S. MART\u00cdN:S. Mart\u00edn is a member of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service working on dysphagia protocols."}{"title": "M. PAREDES:M. Paredes is a member of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service involved in dysphagia care."}{"title": "B. LE\u00d3N:B. Le\u00f3n is a member of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service contributing to dysphagia management."}{"title": "J. F. MERINO:J. F. Merino is a member of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service working on dysphagia protocols."}{"title": "L. GISBERT:L. Gisbert is a member of the Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Service focusing on speech therapy for dysphagia."}{"title": "M. CALATAYUD:M. Calatayud is a member of the Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Service involved in dysphagia rehabilitation."}{"title": "C. BESELER:C. Beseler is a member of the Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Service working on dysphagia protocols."}{"title": "P. ALBARRAC\u00cdN:P. Albarrac\u00edn is a member of the Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Service focusing on dysphagia management."}{"title": "E. VIOSCA:E. Viosca is a member of the Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation Service involved in dysphagia care."}{"title": "D. ESCOLLADO:D. Escollado is a member of the Otolaryngology Service, specializing in dysphagia-related issues. In addition to this focus, D. Escollado is also involved in providing recommendations for medication administration via enteral feeding, indicating a comprehensive approach to managing patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "J. M. PEROLADA:J. M. Perolada is a member of the Otolaryngology Service involved in dysphagia management."}{"title": "C. MORERA P\u00c9REZ:C. Morera P\u00e9rez is a member of the Otolaryngology Service, specializing in treatments related to dysphagia. In addition to this focus, C. Morera P\u00e9rez is also involved in providing recommendations for medication administration through enteral feeding, highlighting a commitment to improving patient care in the context of swallowing disorders."}{"title": "P. MORAL:P. Moral is a member of the Internal Medicine Service who specializes in the care of patients with dysphagia. In addition to providing direct patient care, P. Moral is also involved in making recommendations for medication administration through enteral feeding, ensuring that patients receive appropriate treatment tailored to their needs."}{"title": "I. MORENO:I. Moreno is a member of the Internal Medicine Service who specializes in dysphagia protocols. In addition to this role, I. Moreno is also involved in providing recommendations for medication administration via enteral feeding, ensuring that patients with swallowing difficulties receive appropriate care and treatment."}{"title": "J. L\u00d3PEZ ALDEGUER:J. L\u00f3pez Aldeguer is a member of the Internal Medicine Service, specializing in the management of dysphagia. In addition to this focus, J. L\u00f3pez Aldeguer is also involved in providing recommendations for medication administration through enteral feeding, highlighting a commitment to improving patient care in the context of swallowing difficulties and nutritional support."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE MEDICINA F\u00cd(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO DE ALICANTE:The Hospital General Universitario de Alicante is a prominent healthcare institution that specializes in various medical services. It is home to Dr. \u00c1ngel Luis Abad Gonz\u00e1lez, who serves as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition. Additionally, Dr. \u00d3scar Moreno P\u00e9rez plays a significant role at the hospital, coordinating the Diabetes Unit within the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service. The hospital is also recognized for its commitment to patient care, providing nutritional protocols specifically designed for patients with dysphagia. Overall, the Hospital General Universitario de Alicante is dedicated to delivering comprehensive medical care and specialized services to its patients."}{"title": "GU\u00cdA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N PARA PERSONAS CON DISFAGIA:The guide provides nutritional recommendations for individuals suffering from dysphagia."}{"title": "COMISI\u00d3N DE NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL:The Commission of Artificial Nutrition at HUP La Fe oversees the preparation and administration of enteral nutrition products."}{"title": "J.M. PEROLADA:J.M. Perolada is a professional involved in the recommendations for medication administration via enteral feeding."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES GENERALES PARA LA ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N DE MEDICAMENTOS POR SONDA ENTERAL:General recommendations for the administration of medications through enteral feeding tubes to ensure safety and efficacy."}{"title": "FORMULACIONES EXTEMPOR\u00c1NEAS:FORMULACIONES EXTEMPOR\u00c1NEAS refer to custom-made pharmaceutical preparations that are specifically designed for patients who require enteral nutrition, particularly those receiving medications through enteral feeding tubes. These extemporaneous formulations are essential in ensuring that patients receive the appropriate medication in a suitable form, tailored to their individual needs."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROMES HIPERGLUC\u00c9MICOS:S\u00cdNDROMES HIPERGLUC\u00c9MICOS refers to a category of conditions characterized by elevated blood sugar levels. These conditions may necessitate specific nutritional considerations, particularly in the context of enteral feeding."}{"title": "DIASIP:DIASIP is a nutritional product developed by Nutricia, specifically designed for individuals with hyperglycemic syndromes. It is available in a variety of flavors to cater to different taste preferences and dietary needs."}{"title": "DIBEN DRINK:DIBEN DRINK is a nutritional beverage produced by Fresenius Kabi, designed to cater to individuals with dietary restrictions. It is available in multiple flavors, including lactose-free options, making it suitable for a wide range of consumers."}{"title": "GLUCERNA SR:GLUCERNA SR is a specialized nutritional drink developed by Abbott, specifically formulated for individuals managing diabetes. It is available in a chocolate flavor, among other options, and is designed to meet specific dietary needs."}{"title": "DIASON:DIASON is a nutritional product designed for individuals with specific dietary needs, available in a neutral flavor."}{"title": "IMPACT ENTERAL:IMPACT ENTERAL is a nutritional formula developed by Nestl\u00e9, specifically designed for enteral feeding. It is available in a neutral flavor and is formulated to provide a balanced composition of macronutrients, ensuring adequate caloric intake. The product contains specific nutrients aimed at supporting immune function, making it suitable for individuals requiring specialized nutritional support through enteral feeding."}{"title": "AT\u00c9MPERO:AT\u00c9MPERO is a nutritional product available in various formats and flavors, designed to provide essential nutrients."}{"title": "SURVIMED OPD DRINK:SURVIMED OPD DRINK is a high-protein nutritional beverage formulated to meet specific dietary needs. Manufactured by Fresenius Kabi, it is available in a vanilla flavor and is designed to cater to individuals with particular dietary requirements."}{"title": "ISOSOURCE STANDARD:ISOSOURCE STANDARD is a normocaloric and normoproteic nutritional formula developed by Nestl\u00e9, specifically designed to meet the dietary needs of individuals requiring balanced nutrition. This nutritional product is available in a neutral flavor as well as various other flavors, catering to specific caloric and macronutrient requirements. It is particularly suitable for enteral feeding and is formulated to support patients with unique dietary needs, including those with celiac disease."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS ESPECIALES PARA SITUACIONES DE ESTR\u00c9S O COMPROMISO INMUNOL\u00d3GICO:F\u00d3RMULAS ESPECIALES PARA SITUACIONES DE ESTR\u00c9S O COMPROMISO INMUNOL\u00d3GICO are specialized nutritional formulas designed to support individuals under stress or with compromised immune systems."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA PEPT\u00cdDICA:F\u00d3RMULA PEPT\u00cdDICA is a specialized enteral nutrition formula that contains peptides, specifically designed for patients with cystic fibrosis who experience difficulties tolerating other nutritional formulas. This peptide-based formula is tailored to meet the dietary needs of individuals with specific digestive challenges, as it includes hydrolyzed proteins that facilitate easier digestion and absorption. Overall, F\u00d3RMULA PEPT\u00cdDICA serves as an essential nutritional support option for those requiring specialized dietary interventions."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS NORMOCAL\u00d3RICAS NORMOPROTEICAS:F\u00d3RMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS NORMOCAL\u00d3RICAS NORMOPROTEICAS are nutritional formulas designed to deliver a balanced intake of calories and protein. These formulas are specifically formulated for individuals who require standard nutrition, ensuring that they meet their dietary needs effectively."}{"title": "NUTRISON MULTIFIBRE:Nutrison Multifibre is a nutritional formula designed to provide enteral nutrition with added dietary fiber. It is produced by Nutricia and is available in a neutral flavor, making it suitable for individuals with specific dietary requirements. This product aims to meet the nutritional needs of those who require a fiber-enriched diet."}{"title": "ENSURE HN:Ensure HN is a high-nutritional formula developed by Abbott, specifically designed to meet the dietary needs of individuals with particular health requirements. This nutritional product is available in a vanilla flavor and comes in 500 ml bottles. Ensure HN offers complete and balanced nutrition, making it suitable for patients who require additional support in their diet."}{"title": "HEPATONUTRIL:Hepatonutril is a specialized nutritional formula designed for patients with hepatic encephalopathy, available in biscuit flavor."}{"title": "NEPRO LP:Nepro LP is a specialized nutritional formula developed by Abbott, designed specifically for individuals with pre-dialysis renal insufficiency. This product is available in a vanilla flavor and is intended to support the nutritional needs of patients undergoing pre-dialysis treatment."}{"title": "OXEPA:Oxepa is a specialized nutritional formula developed by Abbott, specifically designed for critically ill patients who require mechanical ventilation and are suffering from acute respiratory insufficiency. This product is available in a neutral flavor and is enriched with antioxidants and omega-3 fatty acids, making it suitable for patients with specific dietary needs in critical care settings."}{"title": "ENSURE PLUS JUCE:Ensure Plus Juce is a nutritional formula available in a bottle, designed to provide essential nutrients without fats, suitable for various dietary needs."}{"title": "NUTRISON LOW SODIUM:Nutrison Low Sodium is a nutritional formula designed for individuals with hypernatremia, available in a neutral flavor."}{"title": "ENSURE PLUS ADVANCE:Ensure Plus Advance is a high-protein nutritional formula manufactured by Abbott, specifically designed to meet the dietary needs of individuals requiring additional support. Available in chocolate flavor as well as various other flavors, this product is formulated to provide essential energy and protein, along with added nutrients, to help individuals maintain their health and well-being."}{"title": "FORTIMEL EXTRA:Fortimel Extra is a high-protein, high-calorie nutritional product developed by Nutricia. It is specifically designed to meet the increased nutritional needs of individuals, offering a rich source of energy and protein. Fortimel Extra is available in a variety of flavors, including Chocolate, Strawberry, and Vanilla, making it a versatile option for those seeking to enhance their dietary intake."}{"title": "PROMOTE:Promote is a nutritional formula available in vanilla flavor, designed to provide essential nutrients with a focus on carbohydrate content."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS PARA SITUACIONES ESPECIALES:F\u00f3rmulas para Situaciones Especiales refers to a category of specialized nutritional formulas tailored for specific medical conditions."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS HIPERPROTEICAS:F\u00f3rmulas Polim\u00e9ricas Hiperproteicas refers to a category of high-protein nutritional formulas designed for individuals requiring increased protein intake."}{"title": "ENSURE PLUS:Ensure Plus is a nutritional product available in raspberry flavor, designed to provide high-calorie intake for individuals needing additional nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRISON ENERGY:Nutrison Energy is a nutritional product developed by Nutricia, specifically designed for enteral feeding. It is available in two bottle sizes, 500 ml and 1000 ml, and offers a high-calorie intake to meet the nutritional needs of individuals requiring specialized dietary support. The product is presented in a neutral flavor, making it suitable for a variety of dietary preferences. As part of Nutricia's product line, Nutrison Energy provides energy-dense nutrition, ensuring that users receive the necessary calories and nutrients for their health and well-being."}{"title": "T-DIET PLUS ENERGY:T-Diet Plus Energy is a high-calorie nutritional product available in vanilla flavor, designed for energy supplementation."}{"title": "RESOURCE INSTANT PROTEIN:Resource Instant Protein is a high biological value protein supplement that can be mixed with various liquids for easy consumption."}{"title": "RESOURCE ARGINAID:Resource ArginAid is a nutritional supplement that contains L-arginine, specifically formulated to be diluted in liquids for consumption. It is designed to deliver arginine, which supports the dietary needs of patients."}{"title": "SCANDISHAKE:ScandiShake is a high-calorie nutritional supplement that can be mixed with milk to enhance caloric intake."}{"title": "NUTRICIONES PARENTERALES ADULTOS:Nutritional protocols for adult patients in the hospital, established in March 2014, focusing on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULOS:Modules refer to specific nutritional supplements that can be added to enhance dietary intake, including protein, arginine, caloric, and thickening agents."}{"title": "PROTEICO:Resource Instant Protein is a high-protein supplement that can be mixed with various liquids to provide additional protein intake."}{"title": "CAL\u00d3RICO:ScandiShake is a caloric supplement designed to provide high energy intake when mixed with milk."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS POLIM\u00c9RICAS HIPERCAL\u00d3RICAS:"}{"title": "ABBOTT NUTRITION:Abbott Nutrition is a company that specializes in nutritional products and solutions for various health needs."}{"title": "BAXTER:Baxter is a global healthcare company recognized for its extensive range of medical products and services. The company has conducted studies focusing on patients receiving Nutritional Parenteral Delivery (NPD), emphasizing various psychosocial aspects and quality of life. As a manufacturer, Baxter is known for producing nutritional solutions, including nitrogenous and lipid solutions specifically designed for parenteral nutrition. Additionally, Baxter has engaged in research that reviews the quality of life of adult patients who are treated with long-term parenteral nutrition, further highlighting its commitment to improving patient outcomes in the healthcare sector."}{"title": "B|BRAUN:B|BRAUN is a company that shares expertise in medical technology and healthcare solutions."}{"title": "NESTL\u00c9 HEALTH SCIENCE:Nestl\u00e9 Health Science is dedicated to nourishing personal health through nutritional science."}{"title": "OLICLINOMEL N4-550 2L:Oliclinomel N4-550 2L is a parenteral nutrition solution designed for patients requiring nutritional support."}{"title": "F. RENAL ANURIA:F. Renal Anuria refers to a medical condition characterized by the absence of urine production, often requiring specific nutritional management."}{"title": "ENCEPHALOPAT\u00cdA HEP\u00c1TICA:Encefalopat\u00eda Hep\u00e1tica is a medical condition related to liver dysfunction that can affect brain function, often requiring specialized nutritional care.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE GERIATR\u00cdA Y GERONTOLOG\u00cdA:The \"Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Geriatr\u00eda y Gerontolog\u00eda\" is a professional society in Spain dedicated to the fields of geriatrics and gerontology. This organization is actively involved in research and education aimed at enhancing the health and well-being of older adults. It focuses on various aspects related to aging, including the promotion of elderly care, addressing issues of frailty, and improving the nutritional needs of the elderly population. Through its initiatives, the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Geriatr\u00eda y Gerontolog\u00eda aims to advance the understanding and management of health care for elderly patients in Spain."}{"title": "DR. MANUEL ANT\u00d3N JIM\u00c9NEZ:Dr. Manuel Ant\u00f3n Jim\u00e9nez is a geriatrician at Hospital Ntra. Sra. de la Monta\u00f1a in C\u00e1ceres. He plays a significant role in the dietary guidelines for older adults, ensuring that their nutritional needs are met. Additionally, he is actively involved in the study and treatment of elderly patients, focusing on their overall health and well-being. Through his work, Dr. Jim\u00e9nez contributes to improving the quality of care for the aging population."}{"title": "DR. I\u00d1AKI ARTAZA ARTABE:Dr. I\u00f1aki Artaza Artabe is a dedicated geriatrician based at Centro Sociosanitario Igurco Orue in Amorebieta, Vizcaya, where he specializes in the care of elderly patients. He has made significant contributions to the guidelines on nutritional assessment specifically tailored for this demographic. In his professional endeavors, Dr. Artaza Artabe collaborates with Dra. Pilar Mat\u00eda Mart\u00edn, focusing on enhancing nutritional assessment practices for the elderly."}{"title": "DR. JOS\u00c9 ANTONIO L\u00d3PEZ TRIGO:Dr. Jos\u00e9 Antonio L\u00f3pez Trigo is a prominent geriatrician and the president of the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Geriatr\u00eda y Gerontolog\u00eda. He is recognized for his significant contributions to the field of geriatrics, particularly in the area of elderly nutrition. Under his leadership, the society has published valuable insights that enhance the understanding and care of the elderly population."}{"title": "DRA. ENCARNA MART\u00cdN P\u00c9REZ:Dra. Encarna Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez is a geriatrician at Hospital San Juan de Dios in Le\u00f3n, focusing on elderly patient care."}{"title": "DR. NICOL\u00c1S MART\u00cdNEZ VELILLA:Dr. Nicol\u00e1s Mart\u00ednez Velilla is a geriatrician at Hospital de Navarra in Pamplona, specializing in the care of elderly patients. He is recognized as an expert in the field of geriatric medicine, particularly for his contributions to the understanding of frailty in the elderly and its implications for healthcare. His work focuses on improving the health outcomes and quality of life for older adults, addressing the complexities associated with aging and frailty."}{"title": "DRA. PILAR MAT\u00cdA MART\u00cdN:Dra. Pilar Mat\u00eda Mart\u00edn is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology at Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario San Carlos in Madrid. She is actively involved in the nutritional assessment and care of fragile elderly patients, focusing on the development and study of nutritional strategies tailored for this vulnerable population. Her work emphasizes the importance of proper nutrition in enhancing the health and well-being of elderly individuals."}{"title": "DR. ROBERTO PETIDIER TORREGROSSA:Dr. Roberto Petidier Torregrossa is a geriatrician at Hospital Universitario de Getafe in Madrid, specializing in elderly care."}{"title": "CENTRO SOCIOSANITARIO IGURCO ORUE:Centro Sociosanitario Igurco Orue is a healthcare facility located in Amorebieta, Vizcaya, where Dr. I\u00f1aki Artaza Artabe works."}{"title": "HOSPITAL SAN JUAN DE DIOS:Hospital San Juan de Dios is a healthcare facility located in Le\u00f3n, where Dra. Encarna Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez provides geriatric care."}{"title": "HOSPITAL DE NAVARRA:Hospital de Navarra is a healthcare facility located in Pamplona, where Dr. Nicol\u00e1s Mart\u00ednez Velilla practices geriatrics."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO SAN CARLOS:Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario San Carlos is a prominent healthcare facility located in Madrid, Spain. It serves as a medical institution specializing in clinical nutrition and endocrinology, among other fields. The hospital is notable for its commitment to providing comprehensive medical services and education. Within this institution, Dra. Pilar Mat\u00eda Mart\u00edn works as an endocrinologist, contributing to the hospital's focus on specialized healthcare."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE GETAFE:Hospital Universitario de Getafe is a healthcare facility located in Madrid, Spain. It is a medical institution where Dr. Roberto Petidier Torregrossa practices geriatrics. Dr. Petidier Torregrosa, who is a geriatrician, is associated with this hospital, contributing to its focus on elderly care."}{"title": "HOSPITAL NTRA. SRA. DE LA MONTA\u00d1A:Hospital Ntra. Sra. de la Monta\u00f1a is a medical institution located in C\u00e1ceres. Within this facility, Dr. Manuel Ant\u00f3n Jim\u00e9nez serves as a practicing geriatrician, providing specialized care for elderly patients."}{"title": "PAUTAS DE INTERVENCI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL EN ANCIANO FR\u00c1GIL:A publication aimed at providing guidelines for nutritional intervention in frail elderly individuals, contributing to the understanding and management of their nutritional needs."}{"title": "ENVEJECIMIENTO Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:\"ENVEJECIMIENTO Y NUTRICI\u00d3N\" refers to a comprehensive series and discussion focused on the relationship between aging and nutrition, particularly emphasizing the dietary needs and nutritional requirements of older adults. This initiative includes a conference or publication that provides nutritional intervention guidelines specifically designed for frail elderly individuals. It aims to promote healthy aging through proper nutrition, offering insights and recommendations for the nutritional management of the elderly population. The series addresses the impact of nutrition on aging and related health issues, highlighting the importance of dietary considerations in the treatment of conditions such as frailty. Additionally, it emphasizes the role of physical activity and adequate caloric and protein intake in maintaining the health and well-being of older adults. Overall, \"ENVEJECIMIENTO Y NUTRICI\u00d3N\" serves as a vital resource for understanding and addressing the nutritional needs of the aging population."}{"title": "ENVEJECIMIENTO SALUDABLE EN TOLEDO:A longitudinal study focused on healthy aging in Toledo, Spain, contributing to research on frailty."}{"title": "ESTUDIO FRADEA:ESTUDIO FRADEA is a research study focused on investigating aspects of fragility among the elderly. It aims to enhance the understanding of aging by analyzing frailty in this demographic, including its prevalence and impact. Through its comprehensive approach, ESTUDIO FRADEA contributes valuable insights into the challenges faced by older adults, thereby advancing knowledge in the field of gerontology."}Nh1␀␀␀␀␀i1␀␀␀␀␀»i1␀␀␀␀␀rj1␀␀␀␀␀k1␀␀␀␀␀§k1␀␀␀␀␀Hl1␀␀␀␀␀␀n1␀␀␀␀␀Wo1␀␀␀␀␀¿p1␀␀␀␀␀Ts1␀␀␀␀␀ít1␀␀␀␀␀çu1␀␀␀␀␀x1␀␀␀␀␀´x1␀␀␀␀␀wy1␀␀␀␀␀=z1␀␀␀␀␀¿|1␀␀␀␀␀m}1␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä1␀␀␀␀␀ºÄ1␀␀␀␀␀zÅ1␀␀␀␀␀ÎÅ1␀␀␀␀␀lÇ1␀␀␀␀␀ÌÇ1␀␀␀␀␀ÑÉ1␀␀␀␀␀Ñ1␀␀␀␀␀äÑ1␀␀␀␀␀ˇÑ1␀␀␀␀␀òÖ1␀␀␀␀␀ôà1␀␀␀␀␀à1␀␀␀␀␀ä1␀␀␀␀␀•ã1␀␀␀␀␀å1␀␀␀␀␀¶å1␀␀␀␀␀Ωé1␀␀␀␀␀Jë1␀␀␀␀␀Àí1␀␀␀␀␀!ì1␀␀␀␀␀≠ì1␀␀␀␀␀î1␀␀␀␀␀}î1␀␀␀␀␀˙î1␀␀␀␀␀ó1␀␀␀␀␀≥ò1␀␀␀␀␀ùö1␀␀␀␀␀õ1␀␀␀␀␀mõ1␀␀␀␀␀8†1␀␀␀␀␀}¢1␀␀␀␀␀L•1␀␀␀␀␀Í•1␀␀␀␀␀≈®1␀␀␀␀␀V©1␀␀␀␀␀Â™1␀␀␀␀␀f´1␀␀␀␀␀¨1␀␀␀␀␀ç¨1␀␀␀␀␀≠1␀␀␀␀␀g≠1␀␀␀␀␀˚≠1␀␀␀␀␀±Æ1␀␀␀␀␀§≤1␀␀␀␀␀6≥1␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ≥1␀␀␀␀␀É¥1␀␀␀␀␀?∂1␀␀␀␀␀‘∏1␀␀␀␀␀øπ1␀␀␀␀␀º1␀␀␀␀␀ º1␀␀␀␀␀hΩ1␀␀␀␀␀∑¡1␀␀␀␀␀í¬1␀␀␀␀␀*«1␀␀␀␀␀¡«1␀␀␀␀␀•Ã1␀␀␀␀␀O‘1␀␀␀␀␀Wÿ1␀␀␀␀␀␀Ÿ1␀␀␀␀␀“€1␀␀␀␀␀∞›1␀␀␀␀␀L‡1␀␀␀␀␀–‚1␀␀␀␀␀q„1␀␀␀␀␀ûÊ1␀␀␀␀␀˘Ë1␀␀␀␀␀:Ï1␀␀␀␀␀ÂÏ1␀␀␀␀␀ˆÓ1␀␀␀␀␀ÑÔ1␀␀␀␀␀-1␀␀␀␀␀”1␀␀␀␀␀ôÒ1␀␀␀␀␀8Ú1␀␀␀␀␀ΩÚ1␀␀␀␀␀nÛ1␀␀␀␀␀)Ù1␀␀␀␀␀ı1␀␀␀␀␀·ı1␀␀␀␀␀rˆ1␀␀␀␀␀b¯1␀␀␀␀␀í¯1␀␀␀␀␀l˘1␀␀␀␀␀(˝1␀␀␀␀␀√˝1␀␀␀␀␀¶ˇ1␀␀␀␀␀c␀2␀␀␀␀␀ì2␀␀␀␀␀)2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀œ2␀␀␀␀␀^2␀␀␀␀␀û
